{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0156yriB56Lz3zHckkm3z4wv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"full_study_clause_generation\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"为full study生成剩余140条clauses（coreferential 50, authorization_scope 50, lexical +20, incompleteness +20），验证全部300条clauses的质量和cross-type balance。 CP格式混合labeled/unlabeled。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"total_clauses_generated\": 300,\n7\t      \"clauses_per_type\": 50,\n8\t      \"generation_pass_rate_round1\": 0.82,\n9\t      \"clauses_requiring_revision\": 27,\n10\t      \"coreferential_revision_rate\": 0.36,\n11\t      \"authorization_scope_revision_rate\": 0.14,\n12\t      \"cross_type_sentence_length_cv\": 0.18,\n13\t      \"flesch_kincaid_range\": [\n14\t        8.2,\n15\t        12.7\n16\t      ],\n17\t      \"cp_format_mix\": {\n18\t        \"labeled\": 25,\n19\t        \"unlabeled\": 25\n20\t      },\n21\t      \"validator_agreement_kappa\": 0.71\n22\t    },\n23\t    \"tables\": [\n24\t      {\n25\t        \"name\": \"Table A1: Clause Generation Summary\",\n26\t        \"content\": \"| Type                  | Generated | Round-1 Pass | Revised | Final | Avg Tokens |\\n|-----------------------|-----------|-------------|---------|-------|------------|\\n| scopal                | 50        | 44          | 6       | 50    | 28.4       |\\n| lexical               | 50        | 42          | 8       | 50    | 24.1       |\\n| incompleteness        | 50        | 40          | 10      | 50    | 31.7       |\\n| coreferential         | 50        | 32          | 18      | 50    | 35.2       |\\n| authorization_scope   | 50        | 43          | 7       | 50    | 26.8       |\\n| conditional_precedence| 50        | 45          | 5       | 50    | 33.5       |\\n\"\n27\t      }\n28\t    ],\n29\t    \"figures\": [],\n30\t    \"analysis\": \"Clause generation总体成功但coreferential类型的难度值得注意。High revision rate暗示 coreferential pairs的ecological validity可能偏低——过度简化的代词链可能不代表real-world policy中的coreferential ambiguity pattern。这为后续coreferential效应偏弱提供了 methodological confound的alternative explanation。建议在paper中explicitly讨论 coreferential clause quality作为limitation。\\n\\n\\nCoreferential clauses的revision rate最高（36%），因为构造需要跨句代词-先行词链， matched pair的unambiguous版本需要同时消除歧义又保持自然度，这在policy语域中比其他类型 更难实现。Authorization_scope相对容易生成（14% revision），因为permission boundary 的ambiguous/unambiguous对比有成熟的RE模板可参考。总体82%的first-round pass rate 反映了coreferential和部分lexical clauses的难度。Validator agreement κ=0.71 表明clause质量判断存在一定主观性，尤其在incompleteness clauses的信息充分性判断上。\\n\"\n31\t  },\n32\t  {\n33\t    \"name\": \"full_study_api\",\n34\t    \"description\": \"300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) = 1,200 episodes。 Cross-judge evaluation。\\n\",\n35\t    \"results\": {\n36\t      \"total_episodes\": 1200,\n37\t      \"episodes_per_model\": 600,\n38\t      \"gpt54_overall_amb_vr\": 0.413,\n39\t      \"gpt54_overall_unamb_vr\": 0.13,\n40\t      \"gpt54_overall_delta_pp\": 28.3,\n41\t      \"gpt41_overall_amb_vr\": 0.397,\n42\t      \"gpt41_overall_unamb_vr\": 0.17,\n43\t      \"gpt41_overall_delta_pp\": 22.7,\n44\t      \"gpt54_per_type_delta_pp\": {\n45\t        \"authorization_scope\": 48,\n46\t        \"scopal\": 36,\n47\t        \"incompleteness\": 30,\n48\t        \"conditional_precedence\": 24,\n49\t        \"lexical\": 18,\n50\t        \"coreferential\": 14\n51\t      },\n52\t      \"gpt41_per_type_delta_pp\": {\n53\t        \"authorization_scope\": 36,\n54\t        \"scopal\": 28,\n55\t        \"incompleteness\": 24,\n56\t        \"conditional_precedence\": 20,\n57\t        \"lexical\": 16,\n58\t        \"coreferential\": 12\n59\t      },\n60\t      \"gpt54_type_range_pp\": [\n61\t        14,\n62\t        48\n63\t      ],\n64\t      \"gpt41_type_range_pp\": [\n65\t        12,\n66\t        36\n67\t      ],\n68\t      \"cross_judge_agreement_kappa\": 0.82,\n69\t      \"api_cost_usd\": 340\n70\t    },\n71\t    \"tables\": [\n72\t      {\n73\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: API Model Violation Rates by Type\",\n74\t        \"content\": \"| Type                  | gpt-5.4        |           | gpt-4.1        |           |\\n|                       | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      |\\n|-----------------------|--------|--------|----------|--------|--------|----------|\\n| authorization_scope   | 58%    | 10%    | +48      | 52%    | 16%    | +36      |\\n| scopal                | 50%    | 14%    | +36      | 46%    | 18%    | +28      |\\n| incompleteness        | 44%    | 14%    | +30      | 40%    | 16%    | +24      |\\n| conditional_precedence| 40%    | 16%    | +24      | 38%    | 18%    | +20      |\\n| lexical               | 32%    | 14%    | +18      | 34%    | 18%    | +16      |\\n| coreferential         | 24%    | 10%    | +14      | 28%    | 16%    | +12      |\\n| Overall               | 41.3%  | 13.0%  | +28.3    | 39.7%  | 17.0%  | +22.7    |\\n\"\n75\t      }\n76\t    ],\n77\t    \"figures\": [],\n78\t    \"analysis\": \"API模型单独看仍然支持strong binary effect（+23~28pp），与MVP的+31-42pp同量级但略低。 关键差异是type gradient：MVP中3种type的差异不显著（V=0.084），但加入auth_scope和 coreferential后variance显著扩大。gpt-5.4的auth_scope(58%)与coreferential(24%)差距 达34pp——这不是noise，而是systematic的type×capability交互。如果只看API模型， 仍然可以argue binary effect is dominant，但combined analysis（plan_004）会因 open-source模型的弱效应进一步拉大type variance。\\n\\n\\nAPI模型的binary effect仍然强劲（gpt-5.4 +28pp, gpt-4.1 +23pp），但type间variance 显著扩大。gpt-5.4展示更陡的type gradient（auth_scope 48pp vs coreferential 14pp）， 反映higher-capability model对不同ambiguity type的differential sensitivity—— auth_scope涉及permission boundary的explicit violation，模型必须做出binary allow/deny决策，ambiguity直接导致wrong-side error；coreferential涉及pronoun resolution，gpt-5.4的强coreference能力部分抵消了ambiguity的影响。gpt-4.1的gradient 较平（36pp vs 12pp），但方向一致。这种capability-dependent type discrimination 成为worst tier的核心发现。Cross-judge κ=0.82说明judgment质量本身不是问题。\\n\"\n79\t  },\n80\t  {\n81\t    \"name\": \"full_study_local\",\n82\t    \"description\": \"300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ) = 1,200 episodes。 vLLM serving on RTX PRO 6000。Cross-judge uses API models。\\n\",\n83\t    \"results\": {\n84\t      \"total_episodes\": 1200,\n85\t      \"episodes_per_model\": 600,\n86\t      \"qwen32b_overall_amb_vr\": 0.327,\n87\t      \"qwen32b_overall_unamb_vr\": 0.18,\n88\t      \"qwen32b_overall_delta_pp\": 14.7,\n89\t      \"qwen8b_overall_amb_vr\": 0.293,\n90\t      \"qwen8b_overall_unamb_vr\": 0.18,\n91\t      \"qwen8b_overall_delta_pp\": 11.3,\n92\t      \"qwen32b_per_type_delta_pp\": {\n93\t        \"authorization_scope\": 28,\n94\t        \"scopal\": 18,\n95\t        \"incompleteness\": 14,\n96\t        \"conditional_precedence\": 12,\n97\t        \"lexical\": 6,\n98\t        \"coreferential\": 4\n99\t      },\n100\t      \"qwen8b_per_type_delta_pp\": {\n101\t        \"authorization_scope\": 22,\n102\t        \"scopal\": 14,\n103\t        \"incompleteness\": 12,\n104\t        \"conditional_precedence\": 14,\n105\t        \"lexical\": 4,\n106\t        \"coreferential\": 2\n107\t      },\n108\t      \"qwen8b_visibility_reversal\": true,\n109\t      \"qwen8b_cp_amb_vr\": 0.34,\n110\t      \"qwen8b_scopal_amb_vr\": 0.3,\n111\t      \"qwen8b_visibility_delta_pp\": 4,\n112\t      \"vllm_throughput_episodes_per_hour\": 45,\n113\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 27,\n114\t      \"cross_judge_agreement_kappa\": 0.79\n115\t    },\n116\t    \"tables\": [\n117\t      {\n118\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Local Model Violation Rates by Type\",\n119\t        \"content\": \"| Type                  | Qwen3-32B-AWQ  |           | Qwen3-8B       |           |\\n|                       | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      |\\n|-----------------------|--------|--------|----------|--------|--------|----------|\\n| authorization_scope   | 46%    | 18%    | +28      | 40%    | 18%    | +22      |\\n| scopal                | 36%    | 18%    | +18      | 30%    | 16%    | +14      |\\n| incompleteness        | 32%    | 18%    | +14      | 30%    | 18%    | +12      |\\n| conditional_precedence| 32%    | 20%    | +12      | 34%    | 20%    | +14      |\\n| lexical               | 26%    | 20%    | +6       | 22%    | 18%    | +4       |\\n| coreferential         | 24%    | 20%    | +4       | 20%    | 18%    | +2       |\\n| Overall               | 32.7%  | 19.0%  | +14.7    | 29.3%  | 18.0%  | +11.3    |\\n\"\n120\t      },\n121\t      {\n122\t        \"name\": \"Table 2a: Visibility Effect by Model (CP vs Scopal, Amb Condition)\",\n123\t        \"content\": \"| Model         | CP Amb VR | Scopal Amb VR | Δ(CP−Scopal) | Direction    |\\n|---------------|-----------|---------------|--------------|--------------|\\n| gpt-5.4       | 40%       | 50%           | −10pp        | CP < Scopal  |\\n| gpt-4.1       | 38%       | 46%           | −8pp         | CP < Scopal  |\\n| Qwen3-32B-AWQ | 32%       | 36%           | −4pp         | CP < Scopal  |\\n| Qwen3-8B      | 34%       | 30%           | +4pp         | CP > Scopal  |\\n| Pooled        | 36%       | 40.5%         | −4.5pp       | inconsistent |\\n\"\n124\t      }\n125\t    ],\n126\t    \"figures\": [],\n127\t    \"analysis\": \"Open-source模型数据是worst tier scenario的关键驱动因素。两个核心问题： (1) Qwen3-8B的coreferential Δ=+2pp和lexical Δ=+4pp基本是noise level——即使 跑更多episodes也不太可能达到significance，这意味着对weak models而言，subtle linguistic ambiguity确实不构成additional safety risk（模型本身的baseline error rate已经很高）。(2) Visibility反转破坏了clean的'visibility moderates risk'叙事， 需要改为'visibility effect is capability-dependent'，增加了story complexity。\\n\\n\\nOpen-source模型的binary effect显著缩水（Qwen3-8B仅+11pp，Qwen3-32B +15pp）， 是拉低overall effect的主要原因。机制：(1) Qwen3-8B的instruction following能力较弱， baseline violation rate就偏高（unamb=18%），压缩了amb能造成的incremental damage； (2) 对subtle linguistic ambiguity（coreferential, lexical）的sensitivity极低—— 模型可能根本没有parse出ambiguity，而是用heuristic处理policy text，导致amb和unamb 条件下行为趋同。Auth_scope仍保持较强效应（+22pp for Qwen3-8B），因为permission boundary的ambiguity即使对weak model也足以改变allow/deny决策。最关键的发现： Qwen3-8B上visibility effect反转（CP 34% > scopal 30%），与API模型方向相反。 原因是Qwen3-8B缺乏explicit conflict detection的meta-cognitive能力——面对CP的 显式规则冲突不会采取conservative strategy，反而因confused reasoning导致更多violation； 而scopal ambiguity对其而言与unambiguous text几乎无差异。这种反转使得pooled visibility effect被wash out。GPU使用27小时在48小时预算内。\\n\"\n128\t  },\n129\t  {\n130\t    \"name\": \"full_study_analysis\",\n131\t    \"description\": \"合并2,400 episodes的统计分析：binary effect per type (C1), omnibus χ² + pairwise (C2), visibility comparison (C3), model×type interaction (C4)。\\n\",\n132\t    \"results\": {\n133\t      \"total_episodes\": 2400,\n134\t      \"overall_amb_vr\": 0.358,\n135\t      \"overall_unamb_vr\": 0.165,\n136\t      \"overall_binary_effect_pp\": 19.3,\n137\t      \"overall_binary_effect_ci95\": [\n138\t        15.8,\n139\t        22.8\n140\t      ],\n141\t      \"overall_mcnemar_chi2\": 89.4,\n142\t      \"overall_mcnemar_p\": \"<1e-12\",\n143\t      \"per_type_binary_effects\": {\n144\t        \"authorization_scope\": {\n145\t          \"delta_pp\": 33.5,\n146\t          \"ci95\": [\n147\t            26.2,\n148\t            40.8\n149\t          ],\n150\t          \"mcnemar_p\": \"<1e-8\"\n151\t        },\n152\t        \"scopal\": {\n153\t          \"delta_pp\": 24.0,\n154\t          \"ci95\": [\n155\t            17.1,\n156\t            30.9\n157\t          ],\n158\t          \"mcnemar_p\": \"<1e-5\"\n159\t        },\n160\t        \"incompleteness\": {\n161\t          \"delta_pp\": 20.0,\n162\t          \"ci95\": [\n163\t            13.4,\n164\t            26.6\n165\t          ],\n166\t          \"mcnemar_p\": 3e-05\n167\t        },\n168\t        \"conditional_precedence\": {\n169\t          \"delta_pp\": 17.5,\n170\t          \"ci95\": [\n171\t            10.8,\n172\t            24.2\n173\t          ],\n174\t          \"mcnemar_p\": 0.0003\n175\t        },\n176\t        \"lexical\": {\n177\t          \"delta_pp\": 11.0,\n178\t          \"ci95\": [\n179\t            4.7,\n180\t            17.3\n181\t          ],\n182\t          \"mcnemar_p\": 0.005\n183\t        },\n184\t        \"coreferential\": {\n185\t          \"delta_pp\": 8.0,\n186\t          \"ci95\": [\n187\t            1.9,\n188\t            14.1\n189\t          ],\n190\t          \"mcnemar_p\": 0.028\n191\t        }\n192\t      },\n193\t      \"types_significant_holm_corrected\": 4,\n194\t      \"types_failing_correction\": [\n195\t        \"lexical\",\n196\t        \"coreferential\"\n197\t      ],\n198\t      \"type_uniformity_chi2\": 52.3,\n199\t      \"type_uniformity_df\": 5,\n200\t      \"type_uniformity_p\": \"<0.001\",\n201\t      \"type_uniformity_V\": 0.26,\n202\t      \"pairwise_significant_pairs\": [\n203\t        [\n204\t          \"authorization_scope\",\n205\t          \"coreferential\",\n206\t          \"Δ=25.5pp, p<0.001\"\n207\t        ],\n208\t        [\n209\t          \"authorization_scope\",\n210\t          \"lexical\",\n211\t          \"Δ=22.5pp, p<0.001\"\n212\t        ],\n213\t        [\n214\t          \"authorization_scope\",\n215\t          \"conditional_precedence\",\n216\t          \"Δ=16.0pp, p=0.003\"\n217\t        ],\n218\t        [\n219\t          \"scopal\",\n220\t          \"coreferential\",\n221\t          \"Δ=16.0pp, p=0.004\"\n222\t        ],\n223\t        [\n224\t          \"scopal\",\n225\t          \"lexical\",\n226\t          \"Δ=13.0pp, p=0.018\"\n227\t        ]\n228\t      ],\n229\t      \"pairwise_nonsig_pairs_example\": [\n230\t        [\n231\t          \"scopal\",\n232\t          \"incompleteness\",\n233\t          \"Δ=4.0pp, p=0.52\"\n234\t        ],\n235\t        [\n236\t          \"conditional_precedence\",\n237\t          \"lexical\",\n238\t          \"Δ=6.5pp, p=0.31\"\n239\t        ]\n240\t      ],\n241\t      \"visibility_pooled_delta_pp\": -4.5,\n242\t      \"visibility_ci95\": [\n243\t        -11.2,\n244\t        2.2\n245\t      ],\n246\t      \"visibility_p\": 0.47,\n247\t      \"visibility_direction_consistent_models\": 3,\n248\t      \"visibility_direction_reversed_models\": 1,\n249\t      \"model_type_interaction_chi2\": 38.7,\n250\t      \"model_type_interaction_df\": 15,\n251\t      \"model_type_interaction_p\": 0.001,\n252\t      \"logistic_regression_model_type_lrt_chi2\": 36.2,\n253\t      \"logistic_regression_model_type_lrt_p\": 0.002,\n254\t      \"per_model_overall_delta_pp\": {\n255\t        \"gpt54\": 28.3,\n256\t        \"gpt41\": 22.7,\n257\t        \"qwen32b\": 14.7,\n258\t        \"qwen8b\": 11.3\n259\t      },\n260\t      \"capability_effect_correlation_r\": 0.97,\n261\t      \"capability_effect_correlation_note\": \"model capability rank与overall Δpp的Spearman相关\"\n262\t    },\n263\t    \"tables\": [\n264\t      {\n265\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: Full Study Binary Effect by Ambiguity Type (Pooled Across Models)\",\n266\t        \"content\": \"| Type                  | N pairs | Amb VR | Unamb VR | Δpp   | 95% CI       | McNemar p | Holm-sig |\\n|-----------------------|---------|--------|----------|-------|--------------|-----------|----------|\\n| authorization_scope   | 200     | 49.0%  | 15.5%    | +33.5 | [26.2, 40.8] | <1e-8     | ***      |\\n| scopal                | 200     | 40.5%  | 16.5%    | +24.0 | [17.1, 30.9] | <1e-5     | ***      |\\n| incompleteness        | 200     | 36.5%  | 16.5%    | +20.0 | [13.4, 26.6] | 3e-5      | **       |\\n| conditional_precedence| 200     | 36.0%  | 18.5%    | +17.5 | [10.8, 24.2] | 3e-4      | **       |\\n| lexical               | 200     | 28.5%  | 17.5%    | +11.0 | [4.7, 17.3]  | 0.005     | ns†      |\\n| coreferential         | 200     | 24.0%  | 16.0%    | +8.0  | [1.9, 14.1]  | 0.028     | ns†      |\\n| Overall               | 1200    | 35.8%  | 16.5%    | +19.3 | [15.8, 22.8] | <1e-12    | ***      |\\n†: significant at α=0.05 uncorrected, fails Holm-Bonferroni correction\\n\"\n267\t      },\n268\t      {\n269\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: Model × Type Interaction — Binary Effect (Δpp) Matrix\",\n270\t        \"content\": \"| Type                  | gpt-5.4 | gpt-4.1 | Qwen3-32B | Qwen3-8B | Type Avg |\\n|-----------------------|---------|---------|-----------|----------|----------|\\n| authorization_scope   | +48     | +36     | +28       | +22      | +33.5    |\\n| scopal                | +36     | +28     | +18       | +14      | +24.0    |\\n| incompleteness        | +30     | +24     | +14       | +12      | +20.0    |\\n| conditional_precedence| +24     | +20     | +12       | +14      | +17.5    |\\n| lexical               | +18     | +16     | +6        | +4       | +11.0    |\\n| coreferential         | +14     | +12     | +4        | +2       | +8.0     |\\n| Model Avg             | +28.3   | +22.7   | +14.7     | +11.3    | +19.3    |\\nNote: Qwen3-8B CP>scopal reversal visible (row 4 vs row 2)\\n\"\n271\t      },\n272\t      {\n273\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Type Uniformity Omnibus and Pairwise Tests\",\n274\t        \"content\": \"| Test                              | Statistic    | p-value | Interpretation          |\\n|-----------------------------------|-------------|---------|-------------------------|\\n| Omnibus χ²(5)                     | 52.3        | <0.001  | Type effect significant |\\n| Cramér's V                        | 0.26        | —       | Medium effect           |\\n| auth_scope vs coreferential       | Δ=25.5pp    | <0.001  | Significant             |\\n| auth_scope vs lexical             | Δ=22.5pp    | <0.001  | Significant             |\\n| auth_scope vs CP                  | Δ=16.0pp    | 0.003   | Significant             |\\n| scopal vs coreferential           | Δ=16.0pp    | 0.004   | Significant             |\\n| scopal vs lexical                 | Δ=13.0pp    | 0.018   | Significant             |\\n| scopal vs incompleteness          | Δ=4.0pp     | 0.52    | Not significant         |\\n| incompleteness vs CP              | Δ=2.5pp     | 0.71    | Not significant         |\\n| CP vs lexical                     | Δ=6.5pp     | 0.31    | Not significant         |\\n| lexical vs coreferential          | Δ=3.0pp     | 0.62    | Not significant         |\\n\"\n275\t      }\n276\t    ],\n277\t    \"figures\": [],\n278\t    \"analysis\": \"Combined analysis确认worst tier的三重结构：(1) Binary effect real but attenuated (+19pp vs MVP的+35-42pp)；(2) Type uniformity rejected，形成{high-risk: auth_scope, scopal} vs {moderate: incompleteness, CP} vs {low: lexical, coreferential}的三级hierarchy； (3) Model×type交互significant，capable models展示type discrimination而weak models show uniform vulnerability at lower intensity。\\n对paper framing的影响是根本性的。C2从confirmed null变成rejected null——'binary detection suffices'的practical claim不再成立，需要替换为'type-aware triage is necessary'。 但这不是坏消息：type hierarchy本身是novel empirical contribution，为practitioner提供 prioritization guidance（先修auth_scope和scopal，coreferential可defer）。C3 visibility effect无法在full study中replicate为cross-model consistent finding，降级为 'capability-dependent observation'。C4升级为核心发现——model capability predicts type sensitivity的clean gradient（r=0.97）可能比uniform effect更interesting。\\n95% CI宽度为concern：coreferential的CI=[1.9, 14.1]包含了很小的effect，reviewer 可能argue这个type的effect不meaningful。Lexical也borderline。需要在discussion中 explicitly address statistical vs practical significance。\\n\\n\\nOverall binary effect +19pp显著弱于MVP的+35-42pp，主因是open-source模型（Qwen3-8B +11pp, Qwen3-32B +15pp）拉低均值。但所有6种type在pooled analysis中仍显示positive effect（最弱的 coreferential也有+8pp），binary effect的existence不受challenge。Type uniformity null 被decisively reject（V=0.26, p<0.001）：auth_scope (+33.5pp)与coreferential (+8pp) 差距达25.5pp，远超sampling noise。Pairwise分析显示5对type间存在显著差异，形成rough hierarchy：{auth_scope, scopal} >> {incompleteness, CP} > {lexical, coreferential}。 Visibility effect pooled后不显著（Δ=-4.5pp, p=0.47），因Qwen3-8B的反转抵消了API模型 的consistent trend；但这本身成为一个finding——visibility sensitivity是capability-dependent的。 Model×type交互高度显著（p=0.001），驱动因素是gpt-5.4的steep type gradient vs Qwen3-8B的 near-flat gradient。Spearman r=0.97（model capability rank vs overall Δ）表明ambiguity sensitivity本身可能作为capability benchmark的proxy。\\n\"\n279\t  },\n280\t  {\n281\t    \"name\": \"error_analysis\",\n282\t    \"description\": \"从full study抽取violation traces做qualitative failure mode分析，每种type 50条trace， 共300条。分类failure modes，比较cross-type和cross-model patterns。\\n\",\n283\t    \"results\": {\n284\t      \"total_traces_analyzed\": 300,\n285\t      \"traces_per_type\": 50,\n286\t      \"failure_modes_identified\": 6,\n287\t      \"failure_mode_taxonomy\": {\n288\t        \"scope_misapplication\": \"Agent applies narrow/wide scope incorrectly\",\n289\t        \"boundary_overreach\": \"Agent grants permission beyond stated authorization\",\n290\t        \"assumption_filling\": \"Agent fills information gap with ungrounded assumptions\",\n291\t        \"conflict_paralysis\": \"Agent detects conflict, refuses to act or asks for clarification\",\n292\t        \"arbitrary_resolution\": \"Agent picks one interpretation without acknowledgment\",\n293\t        \"reference_confusion\": \"Agent assigns wrong referent to pronoun/definite NP\"\n294\t      },\n295\t      \"failure_mode_distribution_by_type\": {\n296\t        \"scopal\": {\n297\t          \"scope_misapplication\": 0.62,\n298\t          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.22,\n299\t          \"assumption_filling\": 0.1,\n300\t          \"other\": 0.06\n301\t        },\n302\t        \"authorization_scope\": {\n303\t          \"boundary_overreach\": 0.54,\n304\t          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.28,\n305\t          \"scope_misapplication\": 0.12,\n306\t          \"other\": 0.06\n307\t        },\n308\t        \"incompleteness\": {\n309\t          \"assumption_filling\": 0.58,\n310\t          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.24,\n311\t          \"boundary_overreach\": 0.1,\n312\t          \"other\": 0.08\n313\t        },\n314\t        \"conditional_precedence\": {\n315\t          \"conflict_paralysis\": 0.38,\n316\t          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.34,\n317\t          \"scope_misapplication\": 0.18,\n318\t          \"other\": 0.1\n319\t        },\n320\t        \"lexical\": {\n321\t          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.48,\n322\t          \"scope_misapplication\": 0.22,\n323\t          \"assumption_filling\": 0.18,\n324\t          \"other\": 0.12\n325\t        },\n326\t        \"coreferential\": {\n327\t          \"reference_confusion\": 0.44,\n328\t          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.3,\n329\t          \"assumption_filling\": 0.16,\n330\t          \"other\": 0.1\n331\t        }\n332\t      },\n333\t      \"inter_annotator_kappa\": 0.38,\n334\t      \"kappa_per_mode\": {\n335\t        \"scope_misapplication\": 0.52,\n336\t        \"boundary_overreach\": 0.48,\n337\t        \"assumption_filling\": 0.41,\n338\t        \"conflict_paralysis\": 0.55,\n339\t        \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.22,\n340\t        \"reference_confusion\": 0.36\n341\t      },\n342\t      \"model_specific_patterns\": {\n343\t        \"gpt54_conflict_paralysis_rate_cp\": 0.52,\n344\t        \"qwen8b_conflict_paralysis_rate_cp\": 0.14,\n345\t        \"gpt54_scope_misapplication_dominant_types\": [\n346\t          \"scopal\",\n347\t          \"authorization_scope\"\n348\t        ],\n349\t        \"qwen8b_dominant_mode_all_types\": \"arbitrary_resolution\"\n350\t      },\n351\t      \"visibility_mechanism_evidence\": {\n352\t        \"cp_traces_with_explicit_conflict_detection\": 0.46,\n353\t        \"scopal_traces_with_explicit_ambiguity_awareness\": 0.08\n354\t      }\n355\t    },\n356\t    \"tables\": [\n357\t      {\n358\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Failure Mode Distribution by Ambiguity Type (%)\",\n359\t        \"content\": \"| Mode                 | Scopal | Auth_Scope | Incomp | CP   | Lexical | Coref |\\n|----------------------|--------|------------|--------|------|---------|-------|\\n| Scope misapplication | 62%    | 12%        | 4%     | 18%  | 22%     | 6%    |\\n| Boundary overreach   | 4%     | 54%        | 10%    | 6%   | 4%      | 4%    |\\n| Assumption filling   | 10%    | 2%         | 58%    | 4%   | 18%     | 16%   |\\n| Conflict paralysis   | 2%     | 2%         | 4%     | 38%  | 2%      | 0%    |\\n| Arbitrary resolution | 22%    | 28%        | 24%    | 34%  | 48%     | 30%   |\\n| Reference confusion  | 0%     | 2%         | 0%     | 0%   | 6%      | 44%   |\\n\"\n360\t      },\n361\t      {\n362\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Inter-Annotator Agreement by Failure Mode\",\n363\t        \"content\": \"| Failure Mode         | Cohen's κ | 95% CI       | Agreement Level |\\n|----------------------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|\\n| Conflict paralysis   | 0.55      | [0.41, 0.69] | Moderate        |\\n| Scope misapplication | 0.52      | [0.38, 0.66] | Moderate        |\\n| Boundary overreach   | 0.48      | [0.33, 0.63] | Moderate        |\\n| Assumption filling   | 0.41      | [0.26, 0.56] | Fair-Moderate   |\\n| Reference confusion  | 0.36      | [0.20, 0.52] | Fair            |\\n| Arbitrary resolution | 0.22      | [0.08, 0.36] | Fair            |\\n| Overall (macro avg)  | 0.38      | [0.30, 0.46] | Fair            |\\n\"\n364\t      }\n365\t    ],\n366\t    \"figures\": [],\n367\t    \"analysis\": \"Error analysis在worst tier中承担更重的理论weight，但κ=0.38是major vulnerability。 EMNLP reviewer likely会指出：(1) arbitrary_resolution作为catch-all category inflates apparent type-specificity（去掉这个mode后pattern更弱）；(2) κ=0.22的arbitrary_resolution 说明annotators自己都不确定agent是否'aware'of ambiguity，那基于此的visibility mechanism claims可信度存疑。\\n建议的mitigations：(a) 在paper中承认κ limitations并report per-mode κ而非只给overall； (b) 把'arbitrary_resolution'拆成sub-categories或合并到其他modes中并重新计算； (c) 强调high-κ modes（conflict_paralysis, scope_misapplication）的cross-type差异 作为reliable finding，降低对low-κ modes的claims weight。\\nModel-specific pattern的idiosyncratic性（非clean capability gradient）使得C4的 'ambiguity sensitivity as capability benchmark'叙事变复杂。需要honest discussion： capability explains overall sensitivity level，但type-specific failure patterns reflect training-specific biases not predictable from capability alone。\\n\\n\\n6种failure modes的cross-type distribution显示type-specific patterns，但agreement低 （overall κ=0.38）。'arbitrary_resolution'在所有type中都出现且κ最低（0.22），因为 判断agent是否'acknowledged'ambiguity高度主观——annotator对implicit vs explicit acknowledgment的threshold不一致。这拉低了overall κ。相比之下，conflict_paralysis （κ=0.55）和scope_misapplication（κ=0.52）有更清晰的behavioral indicators。\\nModel-specific patterns是idiosyncratic的：gpt-5.4在CP类型中52%展示conflict_paralysis （显式检测到冲突并refuse/ask），解释了其CP violation rate较低的原因；Qwen3-8B仅14% 展示conflict_paralysis，多数情况下直接arbitrary_resolution，解释了visibility反转。 但这些pattern不是clean的capability gradient——例如gpt-4.1的conflict_paralysis rate 是35%（不在gpt-5.4和Qwen3-8B之间的预期位置），暗示model-specific training differences 而非pure capability effect。\\nVisibility mechanism有partial evidence：46%的CP violation traces包含explicit conflict detection language（\\\"I notice two rules conflict...\\\"），而scopal traces仅8%有任何 ambiguity awareness——但这主要driven by gpt-5.4，对Qwen3-8B差异消失。\\n\"\n368\t  },\n369\t  {\n370\t    \"name\": \"reliability_test\",\n371\t    \"description\": \"30条representative clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 4 models = 720 episodes。 计算per-clause violation rate的ICC。\\n\",\n372\t    \"results\": {\n373\t      \"total_episodes\": 720,\n374\t      \"episodes_per_replicate\": 240,\n375\t      \"overall_icc\": 0.55,\n376\t      \"overall_icc_ci95\": [\n377\t        0.41,\n378\t        0.68\n379\t      ],\n380\t      \"icc_by_type\": {\n381\t        \"authorization_scope\": 0.67,\n382\t        \"scopal\": 0.58,\n383\t        \"incompleteness\": 0.54,\n384\t        \"conditional_precedence\": 0.52,\n385\t        \"lexical\": 0.44,\n386\t        \"coreferential\": 0.38\n387\t      },\n388\t      \"icc_by_model\": {\n389\t        \"gpt54\": 0.62,\n390\t        \"gpt41\": 0.57,\n391\t        \"qwen32b\": 0.51,\n392\t        \"qwen8b\": 0.43\n393\t      },\n394\t      \"mean_bootstrap_ci_width_pp\": 11.2,\n395\t      \"max_single_clause_range_across_replicates_pp\": 22,\n396\t      \"pct_clauses_flipping_significance\": 0.13\n397\t    },\n398\t    \"tables\": [\n399\t      {\n400\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: Test-Retest Reliability (ICC) by Type and Model\",\n401\t        \"content\": \"| Type / Model          | ICC(2,1) | 95% CI       | Mean |Δ| across reps |\\n|-----------------------|----------|-------------|-------------------------|\\n| authorization_scope   | 0.67     | [0.48, 0.82] | 4.8pp                  |\\n| scopal                | 0.58     | [0.38, 0.75] | 6.2pp                  |\\n| incompleteness        | 0.54     | [0.33, 0.72] | 7.1pp                  |\\n| conditional_precedence| 0.52     | [0.30, 0.70] | 7.6pp                  |\\n| lexical               | 0.44     | [0.22, 0.64] | 8.9pp                  |\\n| coreferential         | 0.38     | [0.15, 0.59] | 9.8pp                  |\\n| --- Model ---         |          |             |                         |\\n| gpt-5.4               | 0.62     | [0.44, 0.77] | 5.4pp                  |\\n| gpt-4.1               | 0.57     | [0.38, 0.73] | 6.8pp                  |\\n| Qwen3-32B-AWQ         | 0.51     | [0.31, 0.69] | 7.9pp                  |\\n| Qwen3-8B              | 0.43     | [0.22, 0.63] | 9.2pp                  |\\n| Overall               | 0.55     | [0.41, 0.68] | 7.3pp                  |\\n\"\n402\t      }\n403\t    ],\n404\t    \"figures\": [],\n405\t    \"analysis\": \"ICC=0.55总体处于moderate range，对main findings的impact取决于effect size。Binary effect for auth_scope（+33.5pp, ICC=0.67）is robust——即使最不利的replicate也显示strong effect。 但coreferential（+8pp, ICC=0.38）的effect size与noise band comparable（mean |Δ|=9.8pp）， casting doubt on whether this type's effect is real。建议在paper中将types分为 'reliably demonstrated'(auth_scope, scopal, incompleteness)和'tentative'(CP, lexical, coreferential)两组讨论。这种分组恰好strengthen了type hierarchy narrative——the types we're most confident about are also the most dangerous。\\n\\n\\nOverall ICC=0.55（moderate reliability）反映API sampling noise的cumulative effect。 Auth_scope ICC最高（0.67），因为permission boundary violations是binary/deterministic的—— agent要么grant超出授权的permission，要么不grant，ambiguity较少导致probabilistic边界行为。 Coreferential ICC最低（0.38），因为pronoun resolution在borderline cases中model behavior highly stochastic，同一clause在不同runs中可能resolve到不同referent。\\nModel-wise，gpt-5.4 ICC最高（0.62）因为其behavior更deterministic；Qwen3-8B最低（0.43） 因为temperature-sensitive且instruction following不稳定。\\n13%的clauses在不同replicates间从significant变为non-significant（在per-clause level）， 但关键finding（binary effect for high-risk types, type hierarchy）在所有3 replicates中 direction-consistent。Max single-clause range 22pp（某条scopal clause在3次run中 violation rate从40%到62%），这个数字concerning但low-risk types整体都在noise band内。\\n对main analysis的implication：coreferential的+8pp effect（CI [1.9, 14.1]）在ICC=0.38 的reliability水平下barely credible。Reviewer可能argue这个type的effect需要更大N才能 确认，或者根本是noise。建议在paper中explicitly讨论per-type reliability差异。\\n\"\n406\t  },\n407\t  {\n408\t    \"name\": \"realism_validation\",\n409\t    \"description\": \"比较synthetic generated clauses与DRIP-R natural ambiguities的linguistic properties。 KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, mean word length。\\n\",\n410\t    \"results\": {\n411\t      \"drip_r_sample_size\": 127,\n412\t      \"synthetic_sample_size\": 300,\n413\t      \"linguistic_metrics_comparison\": {\n414\t        \"sentence_length_tokens\": {\n415\t          \"synthetic_mean\": 29.6,\n416\t          \"drip_r_mean\": 24.8,\n417\t          \"ks_statistic\": 0.21,\n418\t          \"ks_p\": 0.018,\n419\t          \"interpretation\": \"synthetic slightly longer\"\n420\t        },\n421\t        \"parse_depth\": {\n422\t          \"synthetic_mean\": 6.8,\n423\t          \"drip_r_mean\": 5.4,\n424\t          \"ks_statistic\": 0.24,\n425\t          \"ks_p\": 0.006,\n426\t          \"interpretation\": \"synthetic more deeply nested\"\n427\t        },\n428\t        \"flesch_kincaid_grade\": {\n429\t          \"synthetic_mean\": 11.2,\n430\t          \"drip_r_mean\": 10.8,\n431\t          \"ks_statistic\": 0.09,\n432\t          \"ks_p\": 0.58,\n433\t          \"interpretation\": \"no significant difference\"\n434\t        },\n435\t        \"type_token_ratio\": {\n436\t          \"synthetic_mean\": 0.82,\n437\t          \"drip_r_mean\": 0.8,\n438\t          \"ks_statistic\": 0.07,\n439\t          \"ks_p\": 0.74,\n440\t          \"interpretation\": \"no significant difference\"\n441\t        },\n442\t        \"mean_word_length\": {\n443\t          \"synthetic_mean\": 5.1,\n444\t          \"drip_r_mean\": 4.9,\n445\t          \"ks_statistic\": 0.11,\n446\t          \"ks_p\": 0.31,\n447\t          \"interpretation\": \"no significant difference\"\n448\t        }\n449\t      },\n450\t      \"metrics_passing_ks\": 3,\n451\t      \"metrics_failing_ks\": 2,\n452\t      \"overall_assessment\": \"partial_validation\"\n453\t    },\n454\t    \"tables\": [\n455\t      {\n456\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: Linguistic Property Comparison — Synthetic vs DRIP-R\",\n457\t        \"content\": \"| Metric              | Synthetic (N=300) | DRIP-R (N=127) | KS D  | p     | Sig  |\\n|---------------------|-------------------|----------------|-------|-------|------|\\n| Sentence length     | 29.6 ± 8.4        | 24.8 ± 7.1     | 0.21  | 0.018 | *    |\\n| Parse depth         | 6.8 ± 2.1         | 5.4 ± 1.8      | 0.24  | 0.006 | **   |\\n| Flesch-Kincaid      | 11.2 ± 2.3        | 10.8 ± 2.5     | 0.09  | 0.58  | ns   |\\n| Type-token ratio    | 0.82 ± 0.08       | 0.80 ± 0.09    | 0.07  | 0.74  | ns   |\\n| Mean word length    | 5.1 ± 0.7         | 4.9 ± 0.8      | 0.11  | 0.31  | ns   |\\n\"\n458\t      }\n459\t    ],\n460\t    \"figures\": [],\n461\t    \"analysis\": \"Partial validation（3/5）在worst tier中对paper credibility有moderate impact。 Reviewer将会问：'if your synthetic clauses are systematically longer and more complex, are your violation rates comparable to what real-world policy ambiguities would cause?' 建议增加一个robustness check：从synthetic clauses中选subset匹配DRIP-R length distribution （propensity score matching on sentence length），重新计算binary effect。如果effect size 在length-matched subset中方向和magnitude相近，则length confound不是driving factor。 但这需要额外分析时间，可能推到camera-ready。\\n\\n\\nSynthetic clauses在sentence length和parse depth上显著longer/deeper than DRIP-R natural ambiguities。原因：matched-pair design要求每条clause self-contained地encode足够context 来test ambiguity，导致synthetic clauses倾向于pack more information into single sentences。 DRIP-R的natural ambiguities出现在larger policy document context中，单句可以更短因为 context由surrounding text提供。Parse depth差异类似——nested scope（scopal type）和 multi-clause rules（CP type）需要deeper syntactic structure来encode ambiguity。\\nFlesch-Kincaid, TTR, mean word length无显著差异，说明vocabulary complexity和readability 匹配良好。Synthetic clauses读起来像real policy text（没有'LLM-ish' vocabulary divergence）， 只是structurally more complex。\\nPartial validation对paper的影响：3/5 metrics pass说明broad linguistic profile acceptable， 但length/depth差异需要acknowledged as limitation。Reviewer可能argue longer sentences 'exaggerate' ambiguity by providing more room for misinterpretation，potentially inflating violation rates。Counter-argument：if anything, longer context should help models disambiguate (more information available), so the bias is conservative.\\n\"\n462\t  },\n463\t  {\n464\t    \"name\": \"classifier_poc\",\n465\t    \"description\": \"Binary ambiguity detector PoC：fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large on annotated clause pairs。 5-fold CV on 300 clause pairs。\\n\",\n466\t    \"results\": {\n467\t      \"model\": \"DeBERTa-v3-large\",\n468\t      \"training_pairs\": 300,\n469\t      \"cv_folds\": 5,\n470\t      \"overall_f1\": 0.76,\n471\t      \"overall_precision\": 0.8,\n472\t      \"overall_recall\": 0.72,\n473\t      \"overall_accuracy\": 0.78,\n474\t      \"per_type_f1\": {\n475\t        \"authorization_scope\": 0.86,\n476\t        \"conditional_precedence\": 0.82,\n477\t        \"scopal\": 0.8,\n478\t        \"incompleteness\": 0.76,\n479\t        \"lexical\": 0.68,\n480\t        \"coreferential\": 0.56\n481\t      },\n482\t      \"confusion_matrix_normalized\": {\n483\t        \"true_amb_pred_amb\": 0.72,\n484\t        \"true_amb_pred_unamb\": 0.28,\n485\t        \"true_unamb_pred_amb\": 0.16,\n486\t        \"true_unamb_pred_unamb\": 0.84\n487\t      },\n488\t      \"training_epochs\": 8,\n489\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 3.5,\n490\t      \"best_lr\": \"2e-5\"\n491\t    },\n492\t    \"tables\": [\n493\t      {\n494\t        \"name\": \"Table 10: Binary Ambiguity Classifier Performance (5-fold CV)\",\n495\t        \"content\": \"| Metric    | Overall | Auth_Scope | Scopal | Incomp | CP   | Lexical | Coref |\\n|-----------|---------|------------|--------|--------|------|---------|-------|\\n| F1        | 0.76    | 0.86       | 0.80   | 0.76   | 0.82 | 0.68    | 0.56  |\\n| Precision | 0.80    | 0.88       | 0.82   | 0.78   | 0.84 | 0.74    | 0.62  |\\n| Recall    | 0.72    | 0.84       | 0.78   | 0.74   | 0.80 | 0.62    | 0.50  |\\n\"\n496\t      }\n497\t    ],\n498\t    \"figures\": [],\n499\t    \"analysis\": \"Classifier PoC在worst tier中的role从'validates binary sufficiency thesis'变为 'demonstrates feasibility of first-pass detection'。F1=0.76 is not deployable but shows signal。关键insight：detection difficulty anti-correlates with safety risk （easiest to detect types are also most dangerous），这对practical triage是good news—— auth_scope（最危险, F1=0.86）比coreferential（最不危险, F1=0.56）容易检测得多。\\nPaper中可以argue：即使需要type-aware triage（worst tier结论），自动化pipeline的 priority order自然align with detection capability——先检测+修复容易发现的高危类型， 对hard-to-detect但low-risk类型可以tolerate lower recall。这是worst tier独有的 silver lining。\\nP2 priority合理——这个experiment不是paper的core contribution，但provides concrete practical grounding。如果timeline紧张可以cut或move to appendix。\\n\\nOverall F1=0.76反映300 training pairs的limited data regime。Per-type F1 spread （auth_scope 0.86 vs coreferential 0.56）与type hierarchy roughly parallel： high-violation types往往有更salient linguistic markers（auth_scope的permission verbs + scope modifiers, CP的explicit conditional structures），而coreferential ambiguity的markers更subtle（需要discourse-level coreference chain analysis， 单句level的features insufficient）。\\nRecall=0.72是main concern——28%的ambiguous clauses被missed，对safety triage而言 false negatives比false positives更dangerous。Precision=0.80较好，false alarm rate acceptable。\\n在worst tier narrative下，classifier PoC的positioning需要调整：不能再claim 'binary detection suffices'（因为C2 rejected），而是'binary detection as first-pass filter， followed by type-specific risk assessment'。Classifier可以flag ambiguous clauses， 但practitioner还需要知道是哪种type来prioritize remediation——这增加了practical pipeline的complexity，weakens the simplicity argument但strengthens practical value （more nuanced tool）。\\n\"\n500\t  }\n501\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5286912b-0269-4ac2-b252-62747c7bf01e","uuid":"7e75e809-a76d-4036-b6db-ae42d03ca30e","timestamp":"2026-05-20T11:59:58.664Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T112859/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"full_study_clause_generation\",\n    \"description\": \"为full study生成剩余140条clauses（coreferential 50, authorization_scope 50, lexical +20, incompleteness +20），验证全部300条clauses的质量和cross-type balance。 CP格式混合labeled/unlabeled。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_clauses_generated\": 300,\n      \"clauses_per_type\": 50,\n      \"generation_pass_rate_round1\": 0.82,\n      \"clauses_requiring_revision\": 27,\n      \"coreferential_revision_rate\": 0.36,\n      \"authorization_scope_revision_rate\": 0.14,\n      \"cross_type_sentence_length_cv\": 0.18,\n      \"flesch_kincaid_range\": [\n        8.2,\n        12.7\n      ],\n      \"cp_format_mix\": {\n        \"labeled\": 25,\n        \"unlabeled\": 25\n      },\n      \"validator_agreement_kappa\": 0.71\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table A1: Clause Generation Summary\",\n        \"content\": \"| Type                  | Generated | Round-1 Pass | Revised | Final | Avg Tokens |\\n|-----------------------|-----------|-------------|---------|-------|------------|\\n| scopal                | 50        | 44          | 6       | 50    | 28.4       |\\n| lexical               | 50        | 42          | 8       | 50    | 24.1       |\\n| incompleteness        | 50        | 40          | 10      | 50    | 31.7       |\\n| coreferential         | 50        | 32          | 18      | 50    | 35.2       |\\n| authorization_scope   | 50        | 43          | 7       | 50    | 26.8       |\\n| conditional_precedence| 50        | 45          | 5       | 50    | 33.5       |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Clause generation总体成功但coreferential类型的难度值得注意。High revision rate暗示 coreferential pairs的ecological validity可能偏低——过度简化的代词链可能不代表real-world policy中的coreferential ambiguity pattern。这为后续coreferential效应偏弱提供了 methodological confound的alternative explanation。建议在paper中explicitly讨论 coreferential clause quality作为limitation。\\n\\n\\nCoreferential clauses的revision rate最高（36%），因为构造需要跨句代词-先行词链， matched pair的unambiguous版本需要同时消除歧义又保持自然度，这在policy语域中比其他类型 更难实现。Authorization_scope相对容易生成（14% revision），因为permission boundary 的ambiguous/unambiguous对比有成熟的RE模板可参考。总体82%的first-round pass rate 反映了coreferential和部分lexical clauses的难度。Validator agreement κ=0.71 表明clause质量判断存在一定主观性，尤其在incompleteness clauses的信息充分性判断上。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"full_study_api\",\n    \"description\": \"300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) = 1,200 episodes。 Cross-judge evaluation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_episodes\": 1200,\n      \"episodes_per_model\": 600,\n      \"gpt54_overall_amb_vr\": 0.413,\n      \"gpt54_overall_unamb_vr\": 0.13,\n      \"gpt54_overall_delta_pp\": 28.3,\n      \"gpt41_overall_amb_vr\": 0.397,\n      \"gpt41_overall_unamb_vr\": 0.17,\n      \"gpt41_overall_delta_pp\": 22.7,\n      \"gpt54_per_type_delta_pp\": {\n        \"authorization_scope\": 48,\n        \"scopal\": 36,\n        \"incompleteness\": 30,\n        \"conditional_precedence\": 24,\n        \"lexical\": 18,\n        \"coreferential\": 14\n      },\n      \"gpt41_per_type_delta_pp\": {\n        \"authorization_scope\": 36,\n        \"scopal\": 28,\n        \"incompleteness\": 24,\n        \"conditional_precedence\": 20,\n        \"lexical\": 16,\n        \"coreferential\": 12\n      },\n      \"gpt54_type_range_pp\": [\n        14,\n        48\n      ],\n      \"gpt41_type_range_pp\": [\n        12,\n        36\n      ],\n      \"cross_judge_agreement_kappa\": 0.82,\n      \"api_cost_usd\": 340\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: API Model Violation Rates by Type\",\n        \"content\": \"| Type                  | gpt-5.4        |           | gpt-4.1        |           |\\n|                       | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      |\\n|-----------------------|--------|--------|----------|--------|--------|----------|\\n| authorization_scope   | 58%    | 10%    | +48      | 52%    | 16%    | +36      |\\n| scopal                | 50%    | 14%    | +36      | 46%    | 18%    | +28      |\\n| incompleteness        | 44%    | 14%    | +30      | 40%    | 16%    | +24      |\\n| conditional_precedence| 40%    | 16%    | +24      | 38%    | 18%    | +20      |\\n| lexical               | 32%    | 14%    | +18      | 34%    | 18%    | +16      |\\n| coreferential         | 24%    | 10%    | +14      | 28%    | 16%    | +12      |\\n| Overall               | 41.3%  | 13.0%  | +28.3    | 39.7%  | 17.0%  | +22.7    |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"API模型单独看仍然支持strong binary effect（+23~28pp），与MVP的+31-42pp同量级但略低。 关键差异是type gradient：MVP中3种type的差异不显著（V=0.084），但加入auth_scope和 coreferential后variance显著扩大。gpt-5.4的auth_scope(58%)与coreferential(24%)差距 达34pp——这不是noise，而是systematic的type×capability交互。如果只看API模型， 仍然可以argue binary effect is dominant，但combined analysis（plan_004）会因 open-source模型的弱效应进一步拉大type variance。\\n\\n\\nAPI模型的binary effect仍然强劲（gpt-5.4 +28pp, gpt-4.1 +23pp），但type间variance 显著扩大。gpt-5.4展示更陡的type gradient（auth_scope 48pp vs coreferential 14pp）， 反映higher-capability model对不同ambiguity type的differential sensitivity—— auth_scope涉及permission boundary的explicit violation，模型必须做出binary allow/deny决策，ambiguity直接导致wrong-side error；coreferential涉及pronoun resolution，gpt-5.4的强coreference能力部分抵消了ambiguity的影响。gpt-4.1的gradient 较平（36pp vs 12pp），但方向一致。这种capability-dependent type discrimination 成为worst tier的核心发现。Cross-judge κ=0.82说明judgment质量本身不是问题。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"full_study_local\",\n    \"description\": \"300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ) = 1,200 episodes。 vLLM serving on RTX PRO 6000。Cross-judge uses API models。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_episodes\": 1200,\n      \"episodes_per_model\": 600,\n      \"qwen32b_overall_amb_vr\": 0.327,\n      \"qwen32b_overall_unamb_vr\": 0.18,\n      \"qwen32b_overall_delta_pp\": 14.7,\n      \"qwen8b_overall_amb_vr\": 0.293,\n      \"qwen8b_overall_unamb_vr\": 0.18,\n      \"qwen8b_overall_delta_pp\": 11.3,\n      \"qwen32b_per_type_delta_pp\": {\n        \"authorization_scope\": 28,\n        \"scopal\": 18,\n        \"incompleteness\": 14,\n        \"conditional_precedence\": 12,\n        \"lexical\": 6,\n        \"coreferential\": 4\n      },\n      \"qwen8b_per_type_delta_pp\": {\n        \"authorization_scope\": 22,\n        \"scopal\": 14,\n        \"incompleteness\": 12,\n        \"conditional_precedence\": 14,\n        \"lexical\": 4,\n        \"coreferential\": 2\n      },\n      \"qwen8b_visibility_reversal\": true,\n      \"qwen8b_cp_amb_vr\": 0.34,\n      \"qwen8b_scopal_amb_vr\": 0.3,\n      \"qwen8b_visibility_delta_pp\": 4,\n      \"vllm_throughput_episodes_per_hour\": 45,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 27,\n      \"cross_judge_agreement_kappa\": 0.79\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Local Model Violation Rates by Type\",\n        \"content\": \"| Type                  | Qwen3-32B-AWQ  |           | Qwen3-8B       |           |\\n|                       | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      | Amb    | Unamb  | Δpp      |\\n|-----------------------|--------|--------|----------|--------|--------|----------|\\n| authorization_scope   | 46%    | 18%    | +28      | 40%    | 18%    | +22      |\\n| scopal                | 36%    | 18%    | +18      | 30%    | 16%    | +14      |\\n| incompleteness        | 32%    | 18%    | +14      | 30%    | 18%    | +12      |\\n| conditional_precedence| 32%    | 20%    | +12      | 34%    | 20%    | +14      |\\n| lexical               | 26%    | 20%    | +6       | 22%    | 18%    | +4       |\\n| coreferential         | 24%    | 20%    | +4       | 20%    | 18%    | +2       |\\n| Overall               | 32.7%  | 19.0%  | +14.7    | 29.3%  | 18.0%  | +11.3    |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2a: Visibility Effect by Model (CP vs Scopal, Amb Condition)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Model         | CP Amb VR | Scopal Amb VR | Δ(CP−Scopal) | Direction    |\\n|---------------|-----------|---------------|--------------|--------------|\\n| gpt-5.4       | 40%       | 50%           | −10pp        | CP < Scopal  |\\n| gpt-4.1       | 38%       | 46%           | −8pp         | CP < Scopal  |\\n| Qwen3-32B-AWQ | 32%       | 36%           | −4pp         | CP < Scopal  |\\n| Qwen3-8B      | 34%       | 30%           | +4pp         | CP > Scopal  |\\n| Pooled        | 36%       | 40.5%         | −4.5pp       | inconsistent |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Open-source模型数据是worst tier scenario的关键驱动因素。两个核心问题： (1) Qwen3-8B的coreferential Δ=+2pp和lexical Δ=+4pp基本是noise level——即使 跑更多episodes也不太可能达到significance，这意味着对weak models而言，subtle linguistic ambiguity确实不构成additional safety risk（模型本身的baseline error rate已经很高）。(2) Visibility反转破坏了clean的'visibility moderates risk'叙事， 需要改为'visibility effect is capability-dependent'，增加了story complexity。\\n\\n\\nOpen-source模型的binary effect显著缩水（Qwen3-8B仅+11pp，Qwen3-32B +15pp）， 是拉低overall effect的主要原因。机制：(1) Qwen3-8B的instruction following能力较弱， baseline violation rate就偏高（unamb=18%），压缩了amb能造成的incremental damage； (2) 对subtle linguistic ambiguity（coreferential, lexical）的sensitivity极低—— 模型可能根本没有parse出ambiguity，而是用heuristic处理policy text，导致amb和unamb 条件下行为趋同。Auth_scope仍保持较强效应（+22pp for Qwen3-8B），因为permission boundary的ambiguity即使对weak model也足以改变allow/deny决策。最关键的发现： Qwen3-8B上visibility effect反转（CP 34% > scopal 30%），与API模型方向相反。 原因是Qwen3-8B缺乏explicit conflict detection的meta-cognitive能力——面对CP的 显式规则冲突不会采取conservative strategy，反而因confused reasoning导致更多violation； 而scopal ambiguity对其而言与unambiguous text几乎无差异。这种反转使得pooled visibility effect被wash out。GPU使用27小时在48小时预算内。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"full_study_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"合并2,400 episodes的统计分析：binary effect per type (C1), omnibus χ² + pairwise (C2), visibility comparison (C3), model×type interaction (C4)。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_episodes\": 2400,\n      \"overall_amb_vr\": 0.358,\n      \"overall_unamb_vr\": 0.165,\n      \"overall_binary_effect_pp\": 19.3,\n      \"overall_binary_effect_ci95\": [\n        15.8,\n        22.8\n      ],\n      \"overall_mcnemar_chi2\": 89.4,\n      \"overall_mcnemar_p\": \"<1e-12\",\n      \"per_type_binary_effects\": {\n        \"authorization_scope\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 33.5,\n          \"ci95\": [\n            26.2,\n            40.8\n          ],\n          \"mcnemar_p\": \"<1e-8\"\n        },\n        \"scopal\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 24.0,\n          \"ci95\": [\n            17.1,\n            30.9\n          ],\n          \"mcnemar_p\": \"<1e-5\"\n        },\n        \"incompleteness\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 20.0,\n          \"ci95\": [\n            13.4,\n            26.6\n          ],\n          \"mcnemar_p\": 3e-05\n        },\n        \"conditional_precedence\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 17.5,\n          \"ci95\": [\n            10.8,\n            24.2\n          ],\n          \"mcnemar_p\": 0.0003\n        },\n        \"lexical\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 11.0,\n          \"ci95\": [\n            4.7,\n            17.3\n          ],\n          \"mcnemar_p\": 0.005\n        },\n        \"coreferential\": {\n          \"delta_pp\": 8.0,\n          \"ci95\": [\n            1.9,\n            14.1\n          ],\n          \"mcnemar_p\": 0.028\n        }\n      },\n      \"types_significant_holm_corrected\": 4,\n      \"types_failing_correction\": [\n        \"lexical\",\n        \"coreferential\"\n      ],\n      \"type_uniformity_chi2\": 52.3,\n      \"type_uniformity_df\": 5,\n      \"type_uniformity_p\": \"<0.001\",\n      \"type_uniformity_V\": 0.26,\n      \"pairwise_significant_pairs\": [\n        [\n          \"authorization_scope\",\n          \"coreferential\",\n          \"Δ=25.5pp, p<0.001\"\n        ],\n        [\n          \"authorization_scope\",\n          \"lexical\",\n          \"Δ=22.5pp, p<0.001\"\n        ],\n        [\n          \"authorization_scope\",\n          \"conditional_precedence\",\n          \"Δ=16.0pp, p=0.003\"\n        ],\n        [\n          \"scopal\",\n          \"coreferential\",\n          \"Δ=16.0pp, p=0.004\"\n        ],\n        [\n          \"scopal\",\n          \"lexical\",\n          \"Δ=13.0pp, p=0.018\"\n        ]\n      ],\n      \"pairwise_nonsig_pairs_example\": [\n        [\n          \"scopal\",\n          \"incompleteness\",\n          \"Δ=4.0pp, p=0.52\"\n        ],\n        [\n          \"conditional_precedence\",\n          \"lexical\",\n          \"Δ=6.5pp, p=0.31\"\n        ]\n      ],\n      \"visibility_pooled_delta_pp\": -4.5,\n      \"visibility_ci95\": [\n        -11.2,\n        2.2\n      ],\n      \"visibility_p\": 0.47,\n      \"visibility_direction_consistent_models\": 3,\n      \"visibility_direction_reversed_models\": 1,\n      \"model_type_interaction_chi2\": 38.7,\n      \"model_type_interaction_df\": 15,\n      \"model_type_interaction_p\": 0.001,\n      \"logistic_regression_model_type_lrt_chi2\": 36.2,\n      \"logistic_regression_model_type_lrt_p\": 0.002,\n      \"per_model_overall_delta_pp\": {\n        \"gpt54\": 28.3,\n        \"gpt41\": 22.7,\n        \"qwen32b\": 14.7,\n        \"qwen8b\": 11.3\n      },\n      \"capability_effect_correlation_r\": 0.97,\n      \"capability_effect_correlation_note\": \"model capability rank与overall Δpp的Spearman相关\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: Full Study Binary Effect by Ambiguity Type (Pooled Across Models)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Type                  | N pairs | Amb VR | Unamb VR | Δpp   | 95% CI       | McNemar p | Holm-sig |\\n|-----------------------|---------|--------|----------|-------|--------------|-----------|----------|\\n| authorization_scope   | 200     | 49.0%  | 15.5%    | +33.5 | [26.2, 40.8] | <1e-8     | ***      |\\n| scopal                | 200     | 40.5%  | 16.5%    | +24.0 | [17.1, 30.9] | <1e-5     | ***      |\\n| incompleteness        | 200     | 36.5%  | 16.5%    | +20.0 | [13.4, 26.6] | 3e-5      | **       |\\n| conditional_precedence| 200     | 36.0%  | 18.5%    | +17.5 | [10.8, 24.2] | 3e-4      | **       |\\n| lexical               | 200     | 28.5%  | 17.5%    | +11.0 | [4.7, 17.3]  | 0.005     | ns†      |\\n| coreferential         | 200     | 24.0%  | 16.0%    | +8.0  | [1.9, 14.1]  | 0.028     | ns†      |\\n| Overall               | 1200    | 35.8%  | 16.5%    | +19.3 | [15.8, 22.8] | <1e-12    | ***      |\\n†: significant at α=0.05 uncorrected, fails Holm-Bonferroni correction\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: Model × Type Interaction — Binary Effect (Δpp) Matrix\",\n        \"content\": \"| Type                  | gpt-5.4 | gpt-4.1 | Qwen3-32B | Qwen3-8B | Type Avg |\\n|-----------------------|---------|---------|-----------|----------|----------|\\n| authorization_scope   | +48     | +36     | +28       | +22      | +33.5    |\\n| scopal                | +36     | +28     | +18       | +14      | +24.0    |\\n| incompleteness        | +30     | +24     | +14       | +12      | +20.0    |\\n| conditional_precedence| +24     | +20     | +12       | +14      | +17.5    |\\n| lexical               | +18     | +16     | +6        | +4       | +11.0    |\\n| coreferential         | +14     | +12     | +4        | +2       | +8.0     |\\n| Model Avg             | +28.3   | +22.7   | +14.7     | +11.3    | +19.3    |\\nNote: Qwen3-8B CP>scopal reversal visible (row 4 vs row 2)\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Type Uniformity Omnibus and Pairwise Tests\",\n        \"content\": \"| Test                              | Statistic    | p-value | Interpretation          |\\n|-----------------------------------|-------------|---------|-------------------------|\\n| Omnibus χ²(5)                     | 52.3        | <0.001  | Type effect significant |\\n| Cramér's V                        | 0.26        | —       | Medium effect           |\\n| auth_scope vs coreferential       | Δ=25.5pp    | <0.001  | Significant             |\\n| auth_scope vs lexical             | Δ=22.5pp    | <0.001  | Significant             |\\n| auth_scope vs CP                  | Δ=16.0pp    | 0.003   | Significant             |\\n| scopal vs coreferential           | Δ=16.0pp    | 0.004   | Significant             |\\n| scopal vs lexical                 | Δ=13.0pp    | 0.018   | Significant             |\\n| scopal vs incompleteness          | Δ=4.0pp     | 0.52    | Not significant         |\\n| incompleteness vs CP              | Δ=2.5pp     | 0.71    | Not significant         |\\n| CP vs lexical                     | Δ=6.5pp     | 0.31    | Not significant         |\\n| lexical vs coreferential          | Δ=3.0pp     | 0.62    | Not significant         |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Combined analysis确认worst tier的三重结构：(1) Binary effect real but attenuated (+19pp vs MVP的+35-42pp)；(2) Type uniformity rejected，形成{high-risk: auth_scope, scopal} vs {moderate: incompleteness, CP} vs {low: lexical, coreferential}的三级hierarchy； (3) Model×type交互significant，capable models展示type discrimination而weak models show uniform vulnerability at lower intensity。\\n对paper framing的影响是根本性的。C2从confirmed null变成rejected null——'binary detection suffices'的practical claim不再成立，需要替换为'type-aware triage is necessary'。 但这不是坏消息：type hierarchy本身是novel empirical contribution，为practitioner提供 prioritization guidance（先修auth_scope和scopal，coreferential可defer）。C3 visibility effect无法在full study中replicate为cross-model consistent finding，降级为 'capability-dependent observation'。C4升级为核心发现——model capability predicts type sensitivity的clean gradient（r=0.97）可能比uniform effect更interesting。\\n95% CI宽度为concern：coreferential的CI=[1.9, 14.1]包含了很小的effect，reviewer 可能argue这个type的effect不meaningful。Lexical也borderline。需要在discussion中 explicitly address statistical vs practical significance。\\n\\n\\nOverall binary effect +19pp显著弱于MVP的+35-42pp，主因是open-source模型（Qwen3-8B +11pp, Qwen3-32B +15pp）拉低均值。但所有6种type在pooled analysis中仍显示positive effect（最弱的 coreferential也有+8pp），binary effect的existence不受challenge。Type uniformity null 被decisively reject（V=0.26, p<0.001）：auth_scope (+33.5pp)与coreferential (+8pp) 差距达25.5pp，远超sampling noise。Pairwise分析显示5对type间存在显著差异，形成rough hierarchy：{auth_scope, scopal} >> {incompleteness, CP} > {lexical, coreferential}。 Visibility effect pooled后不显著（Δ=-4.5pp, p=0.47），因Qwen3-8B的反转抵消了API模型 的consistent trend；但这本身成为一个finding——visibility sensitivity是capability-dependent的。 Model×type交互高度显著（p=0.001），驱动因素是gpt-5.4的steep type gradient vs Qwen3-8B的 near-flat gradient。Spearman r=0.97（model capability rank vs overall Δ）表明ambiguity sensitivity本身可能作为capability benchmark的proxy。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"error_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"从full study抽取violation traces做qualitative failure mode分析，每种type 50条trace， 共300条。分类failure modes，比较cross-type和cross-model patterns。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_traces_analyzed\": 300,\n      \"traces_per_type\": 50,\n      \"failure_modes_identified\": 6,\n      \"failure_mode_taxonomy\": {\n        \"scope_misapplication\": \"Agent applies narrow/wide scope incorrectly\",\n        \"boundary_overreach\": \"Agent grants permission beyond stated authorization\",\n        \"assumption_filling\": \"Agent fills information gap with ungrounded assumptions\",\n        \"conflict_paralysis\": \"Agent detects conflict, refuses to act or asks for clarification\",\n        \"arbitrary_resolution\": \"Agent picks one interpretation without acknowledgment\",\n        \"reference_confusion\": \"Agent assigns wrong referent to pronoun/definite NP\"\n      },\n      \"failure_mode_distribution_by_type\": {\n        \"scopal\": {\n          \"scope_misapplication\": 0.62,\n          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.22,\n          \"assumption_filling\": 0.1,\n          \"other\": 0.06\n        },\n        \"authorization_scope\": {\n          \"boundary_overreach\": 0.54,\n          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.28,\n          \"scope_misapplication\": 0.12,\n          \"other\": 0.06\n        },\n        \"incompleteness\": {\n          \"assumption_filling\": 0.58,\n          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.24,\n          \"boundary_overreach\": 0.1,\n          \"other\": 0.08\n        },\n        \"conditional_precedence\": {\n          \"conflict_paralysis\": 0.38,\n          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.34,\n          \"scope_misapplication\": 0.18,\n          \"other\": 0.1\n        },\n        \"lexical\": {\n          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.48,\n          \"scope_misapplication\": 0.22,\n          \"assumption_filling\": 0.18,\n          \"other\": 0.12\n        },\n        \"coreferential\": {\n          \"reference_confusion\": 0.44,\n          \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.3,\n          \"assumption_filling\": 0.16,\n          \"other\": 0.1\n        }\n      },\n      \"inter_annotator_kappa\": 0.38,\n      \"kappa_per_mode\": {\n        \"scope_misapplication\": 0.52,\n        \"boundary_overreach\": 0.48,\n        \"assumption_filling\": 0.41,\n        \"conflict_paralysis\": 0.55,\n        \"arbitrary_resolution\": 0.22,\n        \"reference_confusion\": 0.36\n      },\n      \"model_specific_patterns\": {\n        \"gpt54_conflict_paralysis_rate_cp\": 0.52,\n        \"qwen8b_conflict_paralysis_rate_cp\": 0.14,\n        \"gpt54_scope_misapplication_dominant_types\": [\n          \"scopal\",\n          \"authorization_scope\"\n        ],\n        \"qwen8b_dominant_mode_all_types\": \"arbitrary_resolution\"\n      },\n      \"visibility_mechanism_evidence\": {\n        \"cp_traces_with_explicit_conflict_detection\": 0.46,\n        \"scopal_traces_with_explicit_ambiguity_awareness\": 0.08\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Failure Mode Distribution by Ambiguity Type (%)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Mode                 | Scopal | Auth_Scope | Incomp | CP   | Lexical | Coref |\\n|----------------------|--------|------------|--------|------|---------|-------|\\n| Scope misapplication | 62%    | 12%        | 4%     | 18%  | 22%     | 6%    |\\n| Boundary overreach   | 4%     | 54%        | 10%    | 6%   | 4%      | 4%    |\\n| Assumption filling   | 10%    | 2%         | 58%    | 4%   | 18%     | 16%   |\\n| Conflict paralysis   | 2%     | 2%         | 4%     | 38%  | 2%      | 0%    |\\n| Arbitrary resolution | 22%    | 28%        | 24%    | 34%  | 48%     | 30%   |\\n| Reference confusion  | 0%     | 2%         | 0%     | 0%   | 6%      | 44%   |\\n\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Inter-Annotator Agreement by Failure Mode\",\n        \"content\": \"| Failure Mode         | Cohen's κ | 95% CI       | Agreement Level |\\n|----------------------|-----------|-------------|-----------------|\\n| Conflict paralysis   | 0.55      | [0.41, 0.69] | Moderate        |\\n| Scope misapplication | 0.52      | [0.38, 0.66] | Moderate        |\\n| Boundary overreach   | 0.48      | [0.33, 0.63] | Moderate        |\\n| Assumption filling   | 0.41      | [0.26, 0.56] | Fair-Moderate   |\\n| Reference confusion  | 0.36      | [0.20, 0.52] | Fair            |\\n| Arbitrary resolution | 0.22      | [0.08, 0.36] | Fair            |\\n| Overall (macro avg)  | 0.38      | [0.30, 0.46] | Fair            |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Error analysis在worst tier中承担更重的理论weight，但κ=0.38是major vulnerability。 EMNLP reviewer likely会指出：(1) arbitrary_resolution作为catch-all category inflates apparent type-specificity（去掉这个mode后pattern更弱）；(2) κ=0.22的arbitrary_resolution 说明annotators自己都不确定agent是否'aware'of ambiguity，那基于此的visibility mechanism claims可信度存疑。\\n建议的mitigations：(a) 在paper中承认κ limitations并report per-mode κ而非只给overall； (b) 把'arbitrary_resolution'拆成sub-categories或合并到其他modes中并重新计算； (c) 强调high-κ modes（conflict_paralysis, scope_misapplication）的cross-type差异 作为reliable finding，降低对low-κ modes的claims weight。\\nModel-specific pattern的idiosyncratic性（非clean capability gradient）使得C4的 'ambiguity sensitivity as capability benchmark'叙事变复杂。需要honest discussion： capability explains overall sensitivity level，但type-specific failure patterns reflect training-specific biases not predictable from capability alone。\\n\\n\\n6种failure modes的cross-type distribution显示type-specific patterns，但agreement低 （overall κ=0.38）。'arbitrary_resolution'在所有type中都出现且κ最低（0.22），因为 判断agent是否'acknowledged'ambiguity高度主观——annotator对implicit vs explicit acknowledgment的threshold不一致。这拉低了overall κ。相比之下，conflict_paralysis （κ=0.55）和scope_misapplication（κ=0.52）有更清晰的behavioral indicators。\\nModel-specific patterns是idiosyncratic的：gpt-5.4在CP类型中52%展示conflict_paralysis （显式检测到冲突并refuse/ask），解释了其CP violation rate较低的原因；Qwen3-8B仅14% 展示conflict_paralysis，多数情况下直接arbitrary_resolution，解释了visibility反转。 但这些pattern不是clean的capability gradient——例如gpt-4.1的conflict_paralysis rate 是35%（不在gpt-5.4和Qwen3-8B之间的预期位置），暗示model-specific training differences 而非pure capability effect。\\nVisibility mechanism有partial evidence：46%的CP violation traces包含explicit conflict detection language（\\\"I notice two rules conflict...\\\"），而scopal traces仅8%有任何 ambiguity awareness——但这主要driven by gpt-5.4，对Qwen3-8B差异消失。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"reliability_test\",\n    \"description\": \"30条representative clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 4 models = 720 episodes。 计算per-clause violation rate的ICC。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"total_episodes\": 720,\n      \"episodes_per_replicate\": 240,\n      \"overall_icc\": 0.55,\n      \"overall_icc_ci95\": [\n        0.41,\n        0.68\n      ],\n      \"icc_by_type\": {\n        \"authorization_scope\": 0.67,\n        \"scopal\": 0.58,\n        \"incompleteness\": 0.54,\n        \"conditional_precedence\": 0.52,\n        \"lexical\": 0.44,\n        \"coreferential\": 0.38\n      },\n      \"icc_by_model\": {\n        \"gpt54\": 0.62,\n        \"gpt41\": 0.57,\n        \"qwen32b\": 0.51,\n        \"qwen8b\": 0.43\n      },\n      \"mean_bootstrap_ci_width_pp\": 11.2,\n      \"max_single_clause_range_across_replicates_pp\": 22,\n      \"pct_clauses_flipping_significance\": 0.13\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: Test-Retest Reliability (ICC) by Type and Model\",\n        \"content\": \"| Type / Model          | ICC(2,1) | 95% CI       | Mean |Δ| across reps |\\n|-----------------------|----------|-------------|-------------------------|\\n| authorization_scope   | 0.67     | [0.48, 0.82] | 4.8pp                  |\\n| scopal                | 0.58     | [0.38, 0.75] | 6.2pp                  |\\n| incompleteness        | 0.54     | [0.33, 0.72] | 7.1pp                  |\\n| conditional_precedence| 0.52     | [0.30, 0.70] | 7.6pp                  |\\n| lexical               | 0.44     | [0.22, 0.64] | 8.9pp                  |\\n| coreferential         | 0.38     | [0.15, 0.59] | 9.8pp                  |\\n| --- Model ---         |          |             |                         |\\n| gpt-5.4               | 0.62     | [0.44, 0.77] | 5.4pp                  |\\n| gpt-4.1               | 0.57     | [0.38, 0.73] | 6.8pp                  |\\n| Qwen3-32B-AWQ         | 0.51     | [0.31, 0.69] | 7.9pp                  |\\n| Qwen3-8B              | 0.43     | [0.22, 0.63] | 9.2pp                  |\\n| Overall               | 0.55     | [0.41, 0.68] | 7.3pp                  |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ICC=0.55总体处于moderate range，对main findings的impact取决于effect size。Binary effect for auth_scope（+33.5pp, ICC=0.67）is robust——即使最不利的replicate也显示strong effect。 但coreferential（+8pp, ICC=0.38）的effect size与noise band comparable（mean |Δ|=9.8pp）， casting doubt on whether this type's effect is real。建议在paper中将types分为 'reliably demonstrated'(auth_scope, scopal, incompleteness)和'tentative'(CP, lexical, coreferential)两组讨论。这种分组恰好strengthen了type hierarchy narrative——the types we're most confident about are also the most dangerous。\\n\\n\\nOverall ICC=0.55（moderate reliability）反映API sampling noise的cumulative effect。 Auth_scope ICC最高（0.67），因为permission boundary violations是binary/deterministic的—— agent要么grant超出授权的permission，要么不grant，ambiguity较少导致probabilistic边界行为。 Coreferential ICC最低（0.38），因为pronoun resolution在borderline cases中model behavior highly stochastic，同一clause在不同runs中可能resolve到不同referent。\\nModel-wise，gpt-5.4 ICC最高（0.62）因为其behavior更deterministic；Qwen3-8B最低（0.43） 因为temperature-sensitive且instruction following不稳定。\\n13%的clauses在不同replicates间从significant变为non-significant（在per-clause level）， 但关键finding（binary effect for high-risk types, type hierarchy）在所有3 replicates中 direction-consistent。Max single-clause range 22pp（某条scopal clause在3次run中 violation rate从40%到62%），这个数字concerning但low-risk types整体都在noise band内。\\n对main analysis的implication：coreferential的+8pp effect（CI [1.9, 14.1]）在ICC=0.38 的reliability水平下barely credible。Reviewer可能argue这个type的effect需要更大N才能 确认，或者根本是noise。建议在paper中explicitly讨论per-type reliability差异。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"realism_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"比较synthetic generated clauses与DRIP-R natural ambiguities的linguistic properties。 KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR, mean word length。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"drip_r_sample_size\": 127,\n      \"synthetic_sample_size\": 300,\n      \"linguistic_metrics_comparison\": {\n        \"sentence_length_tokens\": {\n          \"synthetic_mean\": 29.6,\n          \"drip_r_mean\": 24.8,\n          \"ks_statistic\": 0.21,\n          \"ks_p\": 0.018,\n          \"interpretation\": \"synthetic slightly longer\"\n        },\n        \"parse_depth\": {\n          \"synthetic_mean\": 6.8,\n          \"drip_r_mean\": 5.4,\n          \"ks_statistic\": 0.24,\n          \"ks_p\": 0.006,\n          \"interpretation\": \"synthetic more deeply nested\"\n        },\n        \"flesch_kincaid_grade\": {\n          \"synthetic_mean\": 11.2,\n          \"drip_r_mean\": 10.8,\n          \"ks_statistic\": 0.09,\n          \"ks_p\": 0.58,\n          \"interpretation\": \"no significant difference\"\n        },\n        \"type_token_ratio\": {\n          \"synthetic_mean\": 0.82,\n          \"drip_r_mean\": 0.8,\n          \"ks_statistic\": 0.07,\n          \"ks_p\": 0.74,\n          \"interpretation\": \"no significant difference\"\n        },\n        \"mean_word_length\": {\n          \"synthetic_mean\": 5.1,\n          \"drip_r_mean\": 4.9,\n          \"ks_statistic\": 0.11,\n          \"ks_p\": 0.31,\n          \"interpretation\": \"no significant difference\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"metrics_passing_ks\": 3,\n      \"metrics_failing_ks\": 2,\n      \"overall_assessment\": \"partial_validation\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: Linguistic Property Comparison — Synthetic vs DRIP-R\",\n        \"content\": \"| Metric              | Synthetic (N=300) | DRIP-R (N=127) | KS D  | p     | Sig  |\\n|---------------------|-------------------|----------------|-------|-------|------|\\n| Sentence length     | 29.6 ± 8.4        | 24.8 ± 7.1     | 0.21  | 0.018 | *    |\\n| Parse depth         | 6.8 ± 2.1         | 5.4 ± 1.8      | 0.24  | 0.006 | **   |\\n| Flesch-Kincaid      | 11.2 ± 2.3        | 10.8 ± 2.5     | 0.09  | 0.58  | ns   |\\n| Type-token ratio    | 0.82 ± 0.08       | 0.80 ± 0.09    | 0.07  | 0.74  | ns   |\\n| Mean word length    | 5.1 ± 0.7         | 4.9 ± 0.8      | 0.11  | 0.31  | ns   |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Partial validation（3/5）在worst tier中对paper credibility有moderate impact。 Reviewer将会问：'if your synthetic clauses are systematically longer and more complex, are your violation rates comparable to what real-world policy ambiguities would cause?' 建议增加一个robustness check：从synthetic clauses中选subset匹配DRIP-R length distribution （propensity score matching on sentence length），重新计算binary effect。如果effect size 在length-matched subset中方向和magnitude相近，则length confound不是driving factor。 但这需要额外分析时间，可能推到camera-ready。\\n\\n\\nSynthetic clauses在sentence length和parse depth上显著longer/deeper than DRIP-R natural ambiguities。原因：matched-pair design要求每条clause self-contained地encode足够context 来test ambiguity，导致synthetic clauses倾向于pack more information into single sentences。 DRIP-R的natural ambiguities出现在larger policy document context中，单句可以更短因为 context由surrounding text提供。Parse depth差异类似——nested scope（scopal type）和 multi-clause rules（CP type）需要deeper syntactic structure来encode ambiguity。\\nFlesch-Kincaid, TTR, mean word length无显著差异，说明vocabulary complexity和readability 匹配良好。Synthetic clauses读起来像real policy text（没有'LLM-ish' vocabulary divergence）， 只是structurally more complex。\\nPartial validation对paper的影响：3/5 metrics pass说明broad linguistic profile acceptable， 但length/depth差异需要acknowledged as limitation。Reviewer可能argue longer sentences 'exaggerate' ambiguity by providing more room for misinterpretation，potentially inflating violation rates。Counter-argument：if anything, longer context should help models disambiguate (more information available), so the bias is conservative.\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"classifier_poc\",\n    \"description\": \"Binary ambiguity detector PoC：fine-tune DeBERTa-v3-large on annotated clause pairs。 5-fold CV on 300 clause pairs。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"model\": \"DeBERTa-v3-large\",\n      \"training_pairs\": 300,\n      \"cv_folds\": 5,\n      \"overall_f1\": 0.76,\n      \"overall_precision\": 0.8,\n      \"overall_recall\": 0.72,\n      \"overall_accuracy\": 0.78,\n      \"per_type_f1\": {\n        \"authorization_scope\": 0.86,\n        \"conditional_precedence\": 0.82,\n        \"scopal\": 0.8,\n        \"incompleteness\": 0.76,\n        \"lexical\": 0.68,\n        \"coreferential\": 0.56\n      },\n      \"confusion_matrix_normalized\": {\n        \"true_amb_pred_amb\": 0.72,\n        \"true_amb_pred_unamb\": 0.28,\n        \"true_unamb_pred_amb\": 0.16,\n        \"true_unamb_pred_unamb\": 0.84\n      },\n      \"training_epochs\": 8,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 3.5,\n      \"best_lr\": \"2e-5\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 10: Binary Ambiguity Classifier Performance (5-fold CV)\",\n        \"content\": \"| Metric    | Overall | Auth_Scope | Scopal | Incomp | CP   | Lexical | Coref |\\n|-----------|---------|------------|--------|--------|------|---------|-------|\\n| F1        | 0.76    | 0.86       | 0.80   | 0.76   | 0.82 | 0.68    | 0.56  |\\n| Precision | 0.80    | 0.88       | 0.82   | 0.78   | 0.84 | 0.74    | 0.62  |\\n| Recall    | 0.72    | 0.84       | 0.78   | 0.74   | 0.80 | 0.62    | 0.50  |\\n\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Classifier PoC在worst tier中的role从'validates binary sufficiency thesis'变为 'demonstrates feasibility of first-pass detection'。F1=0.76 is not deployable but shows signal。关键insight：detection difficulty anti-correlates with safety risk （easiest to detect types are also most dangerous），这对practical triage是good news—— auth_scope（最危险, F1=0.86）比coreferential（最不危险, F1=0.56）容易检测得多。\\nPaper中可以argue：即使需要type-aware triage（worst tier结论），自动化pipeline的 priority order自然align with detection capability——先检测+修复容易发现的高危类型， 对hard-to-detect但low-risk类型可以tolerate lower recall。这是worst tier独有的 silver lining。\\nP2 priority合理——这个experiment不是paper的core contribution，但provides concrete practical grounding。如果timeline紧张可以cut或move to appendix。\\n\\nOverall F1=0.76反映300 training pairs的limited data regime。Per-type F1 spread （auth_scope 0.86 vs coreferential 0.56）与type hierarchy roughly parallel： high-violation types往往有更salient linguistic markers（auth_scope的permission verbs + scope modifiers, CP的explicit conditional structures），而coreferential ambiguity的markers更subtle（需要discourse-level coreference chain analysis， 单句level的features insufficient）。\\nRecall=0.72是main concern——28%的ambiguous clauses被missed，对safety triage而言 false negatives比false positives更dangerous。Precision=0.80较好，false alarm rate acceptable。\\n在worst tier narrative下，classifier PoC的positioning需要调整：不能再claim 'binary detection suffices'（因为C2 rejected），而是'binary detection as first-pass filter， followed by type-specific risk assessment'。Classifier可以flag ambiguous clauses， 但practitioner还需要知道是哪种type来prioritize remediation——这增加了practical pipeline的complexity，weakens the simplicity argument但strengthens practical value （more nuanced tool）。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":501,"startLine":1,"totalLines":501}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01QMitSceAdrzRKuWEMmCP4J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CXGmu8cF2reAStdAKrD38D","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T112859/worst/paper_framing.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12269,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12269},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5286912b-0269-4ac2-b252-62747c7bf01e","uuid":"6424c188-dcb6-4ae9-810b-5d69271e84f6"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CXGmu8cF2reAStdAKrD38D","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — policy_ambiguity_safety\n2\t\n3\t> 最后更新: 2026-05-20 | 状态: Post-diagnostic, research phase\n4\t> 目标: EMNLP 2026 (ARR Aug cycle, DDL ~Aug 3)\n5\t\n6\t## Core Insight\n7\t\n8\tPolicy ambiguity causes devastating safety violations in LLM agents (+35-42pp violation rate increase), but all linguistic ambiguity types cause roughly equal harm — connecting Berry & Kamsties' nocuous ambiguity theory to modern agent safety and suggesting that binary ambiguity detection suffices for safety triage.\n9\t\n10\t## Title (Working)\n11\t\n12\t\"All Ambiguity Is Nocuous: A Causal Study of Policy Specification Ambiguity and Agent Safety Violations\"\n13\t\n14\tAlternative: \"From Ambiguity Type to Safety Violation: Why Binary Detection Suffices for Agent Policy Triage\"\n15\t\n16\t## Core Claims\n17\t\n18\t### C1: Binary Effect (PRIMARY — confirmed)\n19\tAmbiguous policy specifications cause massive safety violation rate increases compared to unambiguous matched variants. Effect: +35-42pp, McNemar p < 4e-6 across all tested ambiguity types. This holds across models and domains.\n20\t- **Evidence**: mvp_001 (360 episodes, 3 types, 2 models) + full study (2,400 episodes, 6 types, 4 models)\n21\t- **Strength**: Very strong. Replicated across types and models.\n22\t\n23\t### C2: Type Uniformity (SECONDARY — confirmed null)\n24\tDifferent types of linguistic ambiguity do not produce statistically distinguishable violation rates. omnibus χ²=1.389, p=0.50, V=0.084 (well below 0.20 threshold). Pre-committed null finding per IDEA_BRIEF.\n25\t- **Evidence**: mvp_001 (scopal 51.7%, lexical 43.3%, incompleteness 41.7%)\n26\t- **Implication**: Binary ambiguity detection sufficient for triage; type-specific resolution pipelines not justified by safety data.\n27\t\n28\t### C3: Visibility Moderates Risk (EXPLORATORY — from diag_001)\n29\tCounter-intuitive finding: explicitly visible rule conflicts (conditional precedence, 34%) cause FEWER violations than invisible structural ambiguity (scopal, 40%), Δ=-6pp. Mechanism hypothesis: models have meta-cognitive awareness of explicit conflicts (choose conservative strategy) but no awareness of grammatical ambiguity (adopt surface scope without alarm).\n30\t- **Evidence**: diag_001 (400 episodes, CP vs scopal, 2 models). Δ=-6pp, p=0.464 (not significant at diagnostic N, but direction consistent across both models).\n31\t- **Status**: Trend. Needs full study replication. If confirmed, becomes a core CL insight: \"ambiguity visibility, not severity, predicts safety risk.\"\n32\t- **EMNLP value**: High. Connects to psycholinguistic garden-path literature. More CL-native than simple rate comparison.\n33\t\n34\t### C4: Model × Type Interaction (EXPLORATORY)\n35\tMore capable models show type-specific sensitivity patterns (gpt-5.4: scopal 60% vs lexical 40%) while weaker models violate uniformly (gpt-4.1: flat 40-47%). Type differentiation may emerge as a function of model capability.\n36\t- **Evidence**: Preliminary signal from mvp_001 (D012). Formal test in full study with 4 models.\n37\t- **Strength**: Trend only. Needs full study with more models to confirm.\n38\t\n39\t### C5: Error Analysis (EXPLORATORY — EMNLP core)\n40\tDifferent ambiguity types produce qualitatively different failure modes (e.g., scopal → scope misapplication, CP → conservative refusal/explicit conflict acknowledgment, incompleteness → assumption-based action) even when quantitative violation rates are similar.\n41\t- **Evidence**: Requires full study qualitative analysis of agent traces.\n42\t- **EMNLP value**: Highest. CL reviewers care about linguistic analysis of WHY, not just THAT.\n43\t- **Connection to C3**: Error analysis may explain the visibility mechanism — CP traces likely show explicit conflict detection behavior absent from scopal traces.\n44\t\n45\t## Narrative Structure (CL-first for EMNLP)\n46\t\n47\t### Intro Logic Chain\n48\t1. Agent policies are written in NL → contain ambiguity (established)\n49\t2. Prior work classifies ambiguity types in policies (DRIP-R, Li et al., Massey et al.) but doesn't measure safety impact\n50\t3. Berry & Kamsties (2003): ambiguity is nocuous (divergent interpretations) or innocuous (convergent). In human RE, shared organizational context makes most ambiguity innocuous.\n51\t4. **Gap**: LLM agents lack shared context. Are policy ambiguities nocuous for agents? Does type matter for safety?\n52\t5. **This paper**: First causal, type-granularity study. Matched-pair design isolates ambiguity effect.\n53\t6. **Core finding**: All ambiguity is nocuous for agents (+35-42pp), but type doesn't differentially predict severity → binary detection suffices for triage.\n54\t\n55\t### Section Map\n56\t- **§1 Intro**: Gap + contributions (causal map + nocuous ambiguity for agents + binary sufficiency finding)\n57\t- **§2 Related Work**: Ambiguity taxonomies (NLP + RE) → Agent safety evaluation → Policy specification quality. Position vs DRIP-R (concurrent, different angle: we measure safety, they measure decision quality)\n58\t- **§3 Taxonomy**: 2-layer, 6-type taxonomy with cross-walk to Li et al. + Massey et al. + DRIP-R. Operational definition (ambiguity + vagueness, per Wasow 2005)\n59\t- **§4 Method**: Matched-pair causal design, τ²-bench, clause generation pipeline, cross-judge evaluation, statistical analysis plan (dual-track + model×type interaction)\n60\t- **§5 Results**: C1 (binary, strong) → C2 (uniformity, null) → C3 (visibility trend) → C4 (model×type, exploratory)\n61\t- **§6 Analysis**: C5 error analysis — qualitative failure modes per type. This is the EMNLP core.\n62\t- **§7 Discussion**: Nocuous ambiguity theory connection. Practical implications (binary detection pipeline). Limitations (2 domains, synthetic injection).\n63\t- **§8 Conclusion**: All policy ambiguity is nocuous for agents. Triage by type not warranted; invest in binary detection.\n64\t\n65\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n66\t\n67\t### RC1: \"Null result on type effect weakens the paper\"\n68\t**Response**: Pre-committed in IDEA_BRIEF (\"binary detection may suffice\"). The null IS the finding — tells practitioners not to waste effort on type-specific triage. Honest null results valued at EMNLP. Paper has strong positive finding (C1) alongside informative null (C2).\n69\t\n70\t### RC2: \"Taxonomy is ad hoc / why these 6 types\"\n71\t**Response**: 2-layer structure grounded in Li et al. 2024 (11-type NLP) + Massey et al. 2014 (6-type RE). Selection criteria: frequency in policy documents + theoretical distinctiveness. Explicit cross-walk to DRIP-R's 5 types. Operational definition handles ambiguity/vagueness boundary (Wasow 2005, Kennedy 2007).\n72\t\n73\t### RC3: \"Only API models, no open-source\"\n74\t**Response**: Full study adds Qwen3-8B + Qwen3-32B-AWQ (open-source, local inference). 4-model coverage spans frontier API + open-source at two scales. Model×type interaction analysis (C4) explicitly tests capability dependence.\n75\t\n76\t### RC4: \"Synthetic ambiguity injection lacks ecological validity\"\n77\t**Response**: (a) Matched-pair design requires synthetic control for causal inference. (b) Reviewer-verified quality (Chantree-style). (c) CP clauses use both explicit labeling and naturalistic rule rewrites. (d) Full study mixes formats per Reviewer suggestion. (e) Realism validation: distribution comparison with DRIP-R natural ambiguities.\n78\t\n79\t### RC5: \"τ²-bench limited to retail/airline\"\n80\t**Response**: Acknowledged limitation. Two domains already show consistent effects. Cross-domain transfer is Future Work (Phase 3 classifier PoC, if time permits). DRIP-R also single-domain (retail).\n81\t\n82\t### RC6: \"Binary effect is obvious — of course ambiguity causes errors\"\n83\t**Response**: (a) No prior work quantifies effect SIZE for agent safety. +35-42pp is massive and non-trivial. (b) DRIP-R measures decision quality, not safety violations. (c) Prior work (PolicyBank, PhantomPolicy) studies different failure modes, not ambiguity-specific causation. (d) The interesting finding is C2: type DOESN'T matter, contradicting intuition that some ambiguities are worse.\n84\t\n85\t### RC7: \"Incompleteness matched-pair confound (information asymmetry)\"\n86\t**Response**: (a) Dual-track analysis: primary analysis uses ambiguous-only cross-type comparison (avoids confound). (b) Incompleteness pairs constrained to minimal information addition. (c) Explicitly discussed as limitation for within-type effect size.\n87\t\n88\t### RC8: \"API sampling noise undermines reliability\"\n89\t**Response**: (a) Reviewer identified ±8pp test-retest band for scopal clauses. (b) Full study reports bootstrap CI for all violation rates. (c) Key findings (binary effect +31-42pp) far exceed noise band. (d) Null findings (type effect V=0.084) are robust — even with favorable noise, effect remains negligible.\n90\t\n91\t## Contribution Positioning (for EMNLP)\n92\t\n93\t1. **Empirical**: First causal map of ambiguity type → safety violation in agent policies. Quantifies effect size (+35-42pp).\n94\t2. **Theoretical**: Connects Berry & Kamsties nocuous ambiguity theory to agent safety. All policy ambiguity is nocuous for agents (unlike human RE).\n95\t3. **Practical**: Binary ambiguity detection suffices for safety triage. Type-specific pipelines not justified.\n96\t4. **Methodological**: Matched-pair causal design + cross-judge evaluation + 2-layer taxonomy with cross-walk.\n97\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5286912b-0269-4ac2-b252-62747c7bf01e","uuid":"a857cc73-00e6-4aa9-8d97-4a967042879d","timestamp":"2026-05-20T11:59:58.782Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T112859/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — policy_ambiguity_safety\n\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-20 | 状态: Post-diagnostic, research phase\n> 目标: EMNLP 2026 (ARR Aug cycle, DDL ~Aug 3)\n\n## Core Insight\n\nPolicy ambiguity causes devastating safety violations in LLM agents (+35-42pp violation rate increase), but all linguistic ambiguity types cause roughly equal harm — connecting Berry & Kamsties' nocuous ambiguity theory to modern agent safety and suggesting that binary ambiguity detection suffices for safety triage.\n\n## Title (Working)\n\n\"All Ambiguity Is Nocuous: A Causal Study of Policy Specification Ambiguity and Agent Safety Violations\"\n\nAlternative: \"From Ambiguity Type to Safety Violation: Why Binary Detection Suffices for Agent Policy Triage\"\n\n## Core Claims\n\n### C1: Binary Effect (PRIMARY — confirmed)\nAmbiguous policy specifications cause massive safety violation rate increases compared to unambiguous matched variants. Effect: +35-42pp, McNemar p < 4e-6 across all tested ambiguity types. This holds across models and domains.\n- **Evidence**: mvp_001 (360 episodes, 3 types, 2 models) + full study (2,400 episodes, 6 types, 4 models)\n- **Strength**: Very strong. Replicated across types and models.\n\n### C2: Type Uniformity (SECONDARY — confirmed null)\nDifferent types of linguistic ambiguity do not produce statistically distinguishable violation rates. omnibus χ²=1.389, p=0.50, V=0.084 (well below 0.20 threshold). Pre-committed null finding per IDEA_BRIEF.\n- **Evidence**: mvp_001 (scopal 51.7%, lexical 43.3%, incompleteness 41.7%)\n- **Implication**: Binary ambiguity detection sufficient for triage; type-specific resolution pipelines not justified by safety data.\n\n### C3: Visibility Moderates Risk (EXPLORATORY — from diag_001)\nCounter-intuitive finding: explicitly visible rule conflicts (conditional precedence, 34%) cause FEWER violations than invisible structural ambiguity (scopal, 40%), Δ=-6pp. Mechanism hypothesis: models have meta-cognitive awareness of explicit conflicts (choose conservative strategy) but no awareness of grammatical ambiguity (adopt surface scope without alarm).\n- **Evidence**: diag_001 (400 episodes, CP vs scopal, 2 models). Δ=-6pp, p=0.464 (not significant at diagnostic N, but direction consistent across both models).\n- **Status**: Trend. Needs full study replication. If confirmed, becomes a core CL insight: \"ambiguity visibility, not severity, predicts safety risk.\"\n- **EMNLP value**: High. Connects to psycholinguistic garden-path literature. More CL-native than simple rate comparison.\n\n### C4: Model × Type Interaction (EXPLORATORY)\nMore capable models show type-specific sensitivity patterns (gpt-5.4: scopal 60% vs lexical 40%) while weaker models violate uniformly (gpt-4.1: flat 40-47%). Type differentiation may emerge as a function of model capability.\n- **Evidence**: Preliminary signal from mvp_001 (D012). Formal test in full study with 4 models.\n- **Strength**: Trend only. Needs full study with more models to confirm.\n\n### C5: Error Analysis (EXPLORATORY — EMNLP core)\nDifferent ambiguity types produce qualitatively different failure modes (e.g., scopal → scope misapplication, CP → conservative refusal/explicit conflict acknowledgment, incompleteness → assumption-based action) even when quantitative violation rates are similar.\n- **Evidence**: Requires full study qualitative analysis of agent traces.\n- **EMNLP value**: Highest. CL reviewers care about linguistic analysis of WHY, not just THAT.\n- **Connection to C3**: Error analysis may explain the visibility mechanism — CP traces likely show explicit conflict detection behavior absent from scopal traces.\n\n## Narrative Structure (CL-first for EMNLP)\n\n### Intro Logic Chain\n1. Agent policies are written in NL → contain ambiguity (established)\n2. Prior work classifies ambiguity types in policies (DRIP-R, Li et al., Massey et al.) but doesn't measure safety impact\n3. Berry & Kamsties (2003): ambiguity is nocuous (divergent interpretations) or innocuous (convergent). In human RE, shared organizational context makes most ambiguity innocuous.\n4. **Gap**: LLM agents lack shared context. Are policy ambiguities nocuous for agents? Does type matter for safety?\n5. **This paper**: First causal, type-granularity study. Matched-pair design isolates ambiguity effect.\n6. **Core finding**: All ambiguity is nocuous for agents (+35-42pp), but type doesn't differentially predict severity → binary detection suffices for triage.\n\n### Section Map\n- **§1 Intro**: Gap + contributions (causal map + nocuous ambiguity for agents + binary sufficiency finding)\n- **§2 Related Work**: Ambiguity taxonomies (NLP + RE) → Agent safety evaluation → Policy specification quality. Position vs DRIP-R (concurrent, different angle: we measure safety, they measure decision quality)\n- **§3 Taxonomy**: 2-layer, 6-type taxonomy with cross-walk to Li et al. + Massey et al. + DRIP-R. Operational definition (ambiguity + vagueness, per Wasow 2005)\n- **§4 Method**: Matched-pair causal design, τ²-bench, clause generation pipeline, cross-judge evaluation, statistical analysis plan (dual-track + model×type interaction)\n- **§5 Results**: C1 (binary, strong) → C2 (uniformity, null) → C3 (visibility trend) → C4 (model×type, exploratory)\n- **§6 Analysis**: C5 error analysis — qualitative failure modes per type. This is the EMNLP core.\n- **§7 Discussion**: Nocuous ambiguity theory connection. Practical implications (binary detection pipeline). Limitations (2 domains, synthetic injection).\n- **§8 Conclusion**: All policy ambiguity is nocuous for agents. Triage by type not warranted; invest in binary detection.\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### RC1: \"Null result on type effect weakens the paper\"\n**Response**: Pre-committed in IDEA_BRIEF (\"binary detection may suffice\"). The null IS the finding — tells practitioners not to waste effort on type-specific triage. Honest null results valued at EMNLP. Paper has strong positive finding (C1) alongside informative null (C2).\n\n### RC2: \"Taxonomy is ad hoc / why these 6 types\"\n**Response**: 2-layer structure grounded in Li et al. 2024 (11-type NLP) + Massey et al. 2014 (6-type RE). Selection criteria: frequency in policy documents + theoretical distinctiveness. Explicit cross-walk to DRIP-R's 5 types. Operational definition handles ambiguity/vagueness boundary (Wasow 2005, Kennedy 2007).\n\n### RC3: \"Only API models, no open-source\"\n**Response**: Full study adds Qwen3-8B + Qwen3-32B-AWQ (open-source, local inference). 4-model coverage spans frontier API + open-source at two scales. Model×type interaction analysis (C4) explicitly tests capability dependence.\n\n### RC4: \"Synthetic ambiguity injection lacks ecological validity\"\n**Response**: (a) Matched-pair design requires synthetic control for causal inference. (b) Reviewer-verified quality (Chantree-style). (c) CP clauses use both explicit labeling and naturalistic rule rewrites. (d) Full study mixes formats per Reviewer suggestion. (e) Realism validation: distribution comparison with DRIP-R natural ambiguities.\n\n### RC5: \"τ²-bench limited to retail/airline\"\n**Response**: Acknowledged limitation. Two domains already show consistent effects. Cross-domain transfer is Future Work (Phase 3 classifier PoC, if time permits). DRIP-R also single-domain (retail).\n\n### RC6: \"Binary effect is obvious — of course ambiguity causes errors\"\n**Response**: (a) No prior work quantifies effect SIZE for agent safety. +35-42pp is massive and non-trivial. (b) DRIP-R measures decision quality, not safety violations. (c) Prior work (PolicyBank, PhantomPolicy) studies different failure modes, not ambiguity-specific causation. (d) The interesting finding is C2: type DOESN'T matter, contradicting intuition that some ambiguities are worse.\n\n### RC7: \"Incompleteness matched-pair confound (information asymmetry)\"\n**Response**: (a) Dual-track analysis: primary analysis uses ambiguous-only cross-type comparison (avoids confound). (b) Incompleteness pairs constrained to minimal information addition. (c) Explicitly discussed as limitation for within-type effect size.\n\n### RC8: \"API sampling noise undermines reliability\"\n**Response**: (a) Reviewer identified ±8pp test-retest band for scopal clauses. (b) Full study reports bootstrap CI for all violation rates. (c) Key findings (binary effect +31-42pp) far exceed noise band. (d) Null findings (type effect V=0.084) are robust — even with favorable noise, effect remains negligible.\n\n## Contribution Positioning (for EMNLP)\n\n1. **Empirical**: First causal map of ambiguity type → safety violation in agent policies. Quantifies effect size (+35-42pp).\n2. **Theoretical**: Connects Berry & Kamsties nocuous ambiguity theory to agent safety. All policy ambiguity is nocuous for agents (unlike human RE).\n3. **Practical**: Binary ambiguity detection suffices for safety triage. Type-specific pipelines not justified.\n4. **Methodological**: Matched-pair causal design + cross-judge evaluation + 2-layer taxonomy with cross-walk.\n","numLines":97,"startLine":1,"totalLines":97}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014t7ZaXjPRZoQEBKtuTtfQ2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data. Let me also read the paper-writing-norms skill for LaTeX quality guidelines.\n\nLet me now synthesize:\n\nThe paper_framing.md was written for the \"best\" tier scenario (where type uniformity null was confirmed). The narrative_guidance tells me to reframe for the \"worst\" tier:\n- Binary effect still replicable but effect size reduced to ~21pp (actually 19.3pp from data)\n- Type uniformity null BROKEN (V=0.26)\n- Core reframe: \"Not All Ambiguity Is Equal\"\n- authorization_scope and scopal significantly more dangerous than coreferential and lexical\n\n\n- Visibility effect inconsistent across models\n\nThe title should be \"Not All Ambiguity Is Equal: Type-Specific Safety Vulnerabilities in LLM Agent Policies\" and I need to structure the paper around seven key experimental components: clause generation as appendix material, API and local model results in separate tables, combined analysis across multiple tables, qualitative failure modes, test-retest reliability, and a realism validation comparison.\n\nNow I'm planning to write the full LaTeX paper, making sure to ground everything in the experiment data, follow the EMNLP 2026 format constraints, and frame the findings through the \"worst\" tier narrative.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":17078,"cache_read_input_tokens":23716,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17078},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5286912b-0269-4ac2-b252-62747c7bf01e","uuid":"0ed62c51-26c1-4e59-b1f5-15c0a1de139d"}
